do_1 = "Give hm-llm a second structured-output surface that can carry one media attachment, alongside the existing text-only LlmProvider::generate_structured. Add crates/hm-llm/src/media.rs declaring MediaModality, MediaAttachment, MediaRequest and the MediaProvider trait, the audio and image media-type allowlists, MAXIMUM_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, and validate_media_request. Implement MediaProvider for OpenAiCompatible<T> in crates/hm-llm/src/openai_compat.rs by building a chat/completions body whose single user message is a content-part array: a text part plus either an input_audio part (base64 data plus a format token) or an image_url part holding a data: URI. Reuse the existing response_format json_schema strict block and the existing luna max_completion_tokens branch by factoring the shared body prefix and the shared choices/usage parsing out of generate_structured so both entry points share one code path."
do_2 = "Author prompts/media-transcript@1.md and prompts/media-description@1.md, whose field vocabulary is fixed in shared_decisions, and update the frozen prompt snapshot test so the registry still passes. Nothing else in the workspace changes: this task only publishes the provider surface that g02-t2 consumes."
do_3 = "Prove it: crates/hm-llm/src/media.rs exists and is declared in crates/hm-llm/src/lib.rs between pub mod gemini; and pub mod ollama;. crates/hm-llm/tests/registry.rs asserts registry.len() == 12 and carries correct blake3 snapshot tuples for ('media-transcript', 1) and ('media-description', 1) in the existing sorted snapshot array."

[task.2.2]
title = "Media derivation contract in hm-cortex with derived_inference provenance"
status = "done"
wave = 2
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = ["2.1"]
reqs = ["2.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/media.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/media.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-cortex --test media"
do_1 = "Add the cognition-side contract that turns retained media bytes into derived text with honest provenance. Create crates/hm-cortex/src/media.rs following the structure of crates/hm-cortex/src/rem/abstract.rs: one request builder per modality, one defensive validator, one response schema, one deterministic call id, one typed drop reason. transcript_request and description_request render the frozen subject facts (media LSN, media type, source URI, digest hex) into a deterministic prompt body and attach the retained bytes as an hm_llm::media::MediaAttachment. derive picks the modality from the media type, refuses an unsupported type before spending a provider call, sends exactly one MediaRequest, parses the response with serde_json::Value accessors only, refuses a refusal or empty text, bounds the text at 64 KiB, and returns a MediaDerivation carrying Authority::DerivedInference, a fully populated ModelProvenance and the provider Usage. This module performs no ledger access and no I/O beyond the provider call; the surface that appends its output is g02-t8."
do_2 = "Prove it: crates/hm-cortex/src/media.rs exists and is declared in crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs in alphabetical position between pub mod ingest; and pub mod nli;. A response whose refusal field is a non-empty string yields Err(MediaDropReason::Refused(_)); empty or whitespace-only text yields Err(MediaDropReason::EmptyText); text longer than 65536 bytes or text for which hm_compose-style raw wire prefixes apply is rejected; a response missing a required field or carrying confidence_micros outside 0..=1_000_000 yields Err(MediaDropReason::Schema(_))."

[task.2.3]
title = "Authorized web-source fetch with crawl policy, private-address refusal and validated redirects"
status = "done"
wave = 2
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = []
reqs = ["2.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/websource.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/web_source.rs", "docs/guides/operations.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test web_source"
do_1 = "Add the hardened retrieval component that every web source must pass through. Create crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/websource.rs holding CrawlPolicy, the FetchTransport trait with a real blocking HttpFetchTransport and a deterministic RecordedFetchTransport, the pure policy functions, and WebSourceRuntime which composes them. The crawl policy is explicit: an operator-declared host allowlist, a response-size limit, a redirect budget, a per-host minimum interval and a switch for cross-host redirects."
do_2 = "Automatic redirect following is disabled in the reqwest client; the runtime follows Location headers itself and re-runs the full target validation on every hop, so a redirect into a private address or an unlisted host is refused rather than followed. Refusal of private and otherwise non-routable destinations is decided on literal IPs in the URL and on every address the host resolves to before the request is issued. The fetch result records the final URL, the normalised MIME type, the HTTP status, the redirect chain, the body and its blake3 digest."
do_3 = "This task appends nothing to the ledger; the consumer is g02-t5."
do_4 = "Prove it: crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/websource.rs exists and is declared in crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs in alphabetical position after pub mod retract;. WebSourceRuntime enforces CrawlPolicy::minimum_interval_ms per final-URL host by sleeping the remaining interval before issuing a request."

[task.2.4]
title = "Bounded text extraction from fetched web payloads"
status = "done"
wave = 2
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = []
reqs = ["2.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/webtext.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/web_text.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test web_text"
do_1 = "Add the deterministic, dependency-free extraction step that turns a fetched textual payload into indexable text. Create crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/webtext.rs with is_textual and extract_text. extract_text accepts text/html, application/xhtml+xml, text/plain, text/markdown, text/csv and application/json, refuses every other media type with ErrorCode::OperationUnavailable, refuses non-UTF-8 bytes with ErrorCode::SchemaInvalid and refuses payloads whose extracted text exceeds MAXIMUM_EXTRACTED_BYTES with ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded. HTML extraction removes script and style element contents and comments, captures the first title element, turns block-level element ends into line breaks, strips every remaining tag, decodes the named entities amp, lt, gt, quot, apos and nbsp plus decimal and hexadecimal numeric references, collapses whitespace runs and trims."
do_2 = "Extraction is pure: no network, no allocation of more than the payload, no dependency added. The consumer is g02-t5."
do_3 = "Prove it: crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/webtext.rs exists and is declared in crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs in alphabetical position after pub mod websource;. extract_text is byte-identical across two invocations on the same input and allocates no global state."

[task.2.5]
title = "remember gains an authorized web-source surface that retains the original and records MIME and final URL"
status = "done"
wave = 2
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["2.3", "2.4"]
reqs = ["2.1", "2.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/websource.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/web_source_surface.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test web_source_surface"
do_1 = "Wire the fetch and extraction components into the existing remember verb as a new argument surface, without adding an MCP verb. RememberInput gains an optional source object; exactly one of content and source must be supplied. When source is present the server fetches through the WebSourceRuntime on a blocking thread, then appends one batch containing: a MediaRef event in the caller's conversation carrying the final URL, the normalised MIME type and the blake3 digest; a ProviderFrame event in the digest-derived media conversation retaining the response bytes verbatim under the provider label hm-web-source@1; and, when the media type is textual, the extracted text chunked with the existing chunk_text into UserMsg events in the caller's conversation with ExternalObserved authority."
do_2 = "Existing embedding behaviour is reused for the text chunks. When the media type is not textual, no text event is written and the envelope reports a media_derivation_pending gap naming the MediaRef LSN. The runtime is threaded through McpToolDispatcher exactly as the embedding, reconstruction and consolidation runtimes already are."
do_3 = "Prove it: RememberInput carries #[serde(default)] pub content: String and #[serde(default)] pub source: Option<RememberSource>; supplying both, or neither, returns ErrorCode::InvalidArgument; existing callers that send only content behave exactly as before and every existing crates/hm-mcp test stays green. McpServer gains a web_source_runtime field with with_web_source_runtime, and McpToolDispatcher gains the matching field populated by from_env from websource::policy_from_env; when the policy is absent the field is None."

[task.2.6]
title = "Media catalog projection rebuilt from MediaRef, retention and derivation events"
