do_1 = "Add the read model that answers what media the actor holds and which items still await derivation. Append ProjectionId::MediaCatalog and its name media_catalog, bump ProjectionId::COUNT to 19, and create crates/hm-proj/src/media.rs following crates/hm-proj/src/attestations.rs end to end. The projection applies MediaRef events by writing a record keyed by digest, a pending marker, and two call-id index entries computed with the same domain-separated blake3 rule that hm-cortex uses, so a later derived event can be joined back without any schema field."
do_2 = "It applies ProviderFrame events by hashing api_content and, when that digest names a known record, recording the retention LSN. It applies UserMsg events whose envelope authority is DerivedInference and whose model_provenance carries a 32-byte call_id by resolving that call id to a digest and recording the derivation LSN and prompt id, clearing the pending marker. Every other kind advances the checkpoint with an empty apply. Register the projection in the rebuild stream and in reset_all so a full rebuild is byte-identical."
do_3 = "The consumer is g02-t7."
do_4 = "Prove it: crates/hm-proj/src/store.rs declares ProjectionId::MediaCatalog as the last variant, PROJECTION_NAMES ends with 'media_catalog' at the matching index, and ProjectionId::COUNT is 19. A full reset rebuild of the same frame vector twice yields byte-identical ReadSnapshot::canonical_dump(ProjectionId::MediaCatalog)."

