do_1 = "Surface the media catalog through the existing inspect verb so an operator can see what media is held and what still awaits derivation, without adding an MCP verb. Add a MediaCatalog command to ActorEngine following the existing AttentionHistory and Procedures commands: a variant on the Command enum, an async accessor on ActorEngine, and a writer-side handler that opens a read snapshot and calls MediaCatalogProjection::list or ::pending. Extend crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs with two URI branches that return the catalog rows on the existing envelope, each row carrying the digest hex, the source URI, the media type, the MediaRef LSN, the retention LSN, the derivation LSN and its prompt id, with hm:// provenance for every referenced LSN. Both branches are read-only and touch no provider."
do_2 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::media_catalog(pending_only: bool, limit: usize) exists and is served by a Command::MediaCatalog variant handled in the writer loop with a read snapshot, returning ErrorCode::InvalidArgument for limit == 0 and capping limit at 256. No LLM provider, embedder or network call is made on either branch."

[task.2.8]
title = "remember gains an explicit media derivation job producing derived_inference transcripts and descriptions"
status = "done"
wave = 2
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["2.2", "2.7"]
reqs = ["2.3", "2.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/media.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/media_derivation.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/fixtures/media-derivation-centra.json", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/concepts/authority.md", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test media_derivation"
do_1 = "Close the vertical by adding the explicit background job that makes retained media searchable. RememberInput gains an optional derive object naming the MediaRef LSN to derive. The job reads that MediaRef frame from the ledger, recovers the digest, media type and source URI, locates the retained ProviderFrame in the digest-derived media conversation, and runs hm_cortex::media::derive on a blocking thread through a MediaRuntime built from HM_MEDIA_PROVIDER. The returned text is appended as UserMsg chunks in the caller's conversation with Authority::DerivedInference and the derivation's ModelProvenance on every chunk, then embedded through the existing embedding path so the media becomes lexically and semantically recallable."
do_2 = "The media catalog is the idempotency guard: when the record already carries a derivation LSN the job returns the existing result without spending a provider call. The job is reachable only through remember, never through recall or activate, so the model-free foreground contract is preserved."
do_3 = "Prove it: RememberInput carries #[serde(default)] pub derive: Option<RememberDerive>; content, source and derive are mutually exclusive and supplying more than one, or none, returns ErrorCode::InvalidArgument. docs/tools/usage.json tools.remember and docs/reference/mcp.md document the derive surface, and the regenerated catalogs are committed."

[task.3.1]
title = "Deterministic repository snapshot reader in hm-cortex"
status = "done"
wave = 3
section = "Wave 3 - Repository graph: a caller-supplied snapshot, deterministically derived and traversable"
owner_lane = "cognition"
requires = []
reqs = ["3.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/repograph.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/repograph.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test repograph"
do_1 = "Add crates/hm-cortex/src/repograph.rs, a pure, LLM-free reader for a caller-supplied repository snapshot document, in the style of the crate's other deterministic modules (nrem/cluster.rs, procedures.rs): no I/O, no provider, no ledger. The document is newline-delimited JSON: the first line of the first shard is a header object carrying contract, repository and fact_count; every later non-empty line is one repository fact with kind, name and optional path, line, end_line, attributes and relations. parse_snapshot takes the ordered shards as they were observed in the ledger (lsn plus content bytes), validates the header, parses every fact line, and records for each surviving fact the exact byte range of its line inside its shard so later stages can cite real observed bytes. Unknown fact kinds, malformed lines, empty or oversized names and malformed relation entries are counted in skipped and dropped; a wrong contract, a non-UTF-8 shard, a fact-count mismatch or more than MAXIMUM_SNAPSHOT_FACTS lines fail closed with a typed error."
do_2 = "Facts are ordered by (kind, name, lsn, byte_start) and duplicate (kind, name) pairs collapse to the first occurrence, so two parses of the same bytes produce byte-identical output. This task also defines node identity and the canonical node rendering (display name, definition bytes, tags) that task g03-t7 turns into memory records; its consumer is g03-t2 and g03-t7 in this group."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_cortex::repograph::parse_snapshot accepts a two-shard snapshot carrying one fact of each of the six kinds and returns six facts, the declared repository, the snapshot digest and skipped == 0. Parsing the same bytes twice yields identical facts ordering, identical digests and identical node ids."

[task.3.2]
title = "Relation resolution into validated repository edges"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "cognition"
requires = ["3.1"]
reqs = ["3.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/repograph.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/repograph_edges.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test repograph_edges"
do_1 = "Extend crates/hm-cortex/src/repograph.rs with resolve, the deterministic step that turns parsed facts into the node and edge lists the ledger will carry. Every fact becomes one RepoNode with its node id, display name, definition bytes, tags and its citation. Every declared relation is resolved against the same snapshot: first by exact fact name, then, when no fact carries that exact name, by a unique suffix match after the last / or . so a bare target name still binds; ambiguity resolves to nothing and is dropped with a reason rather than bound to an arbitrary fact."
do_2 = "Relations outside the eight-name vocabulary, targets that do not resolve, and relations whose resolved target equals their source (which validate_edge_asserted forbids) are dropped into a typed RepoDrop list. Repeated (source, relation, target) triples collapse into one edge whose weight_micros counts the distinct declaring facts. Nodes and edges are emitted in a fixed order with fixed caps, so the ledger event stream for one snapshot is byte-identical on every run; the consumer is g03-t7 in this group."
do_3 = "Prove it: resolve returns one RepoNode per surviving fact, in (kind, name) order, each carrying node_id, display_name, definition, non-empty tags and the fact's citation. Resolving the same snapshot twice yields identical node ids, edge ids, ordering and drop lists."

[task.3.3]
title = "Admit zero-cost provenance for the pinned deterministic extraction identity"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "schema"
requires = []
reqs = ["3.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs", "crates/hm-schema/tests/validation.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-schema --test validation"
do_1 = "Derived kinds (MemoryMinted, MemoryRevised, EdgeAsserted, EdgeRetracted) must carry model_provenance whose token counts are non-zero, unless the envelope matches the one deterministic producer already pinned in validate_envelope (crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs:384). A repository graph is derived without any model call, so this task adds a second pinned producer beside that one rather than letting any zero-token provenance through. Add the public contract constants for the snapshot carrier and the extraction identity, and a private is_repository_extraction predicate that admits a zero-token, zero-cost provenance only when every field of the identity matches exactly: the derived kind, Authority::DerivedInference, the model id, the prompt id, prompt version 1, temperature 0.0, all four token counters and the cost at zero, a 32-byte call_id, and a run_id that is exactly the run prefix followed by the lowercase hex of that call_id."
do_2 = "Nothing else in admission changes: a generic zero-token derived envelope is still rejected with SchemaInvalid, and no new event kind, union member, error code or schema file is touched. The consumers are g03-t4 (the carrier constant) and g03-t7 (the extraction identity)."
do_3 = "Prove it: An EdgeAsserted envelope carrying the pinned identity verifies at Boundary::Disk, Boundary::Socket and Boundary::Import. cargo test -p hm-schema --test validation passes, including every test that was already there."

[task.3.4]
title = "Repository snapshot frames feed the entity projection"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "projections"
requires = ["3.3"]
reqs = ["3.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/entities.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/entities.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --test entities"
do_1 = "The entity projection today indexes only UserMsg and DeliveredMsg payloads (crates/hm-proj/src/entities.rs:89), so an externally observed repository snapshot sitting in the ledger is invisible to entity recall. Extend its document_text helper so a ProviderFrame whose provider equals hm_schema::event::REPOSITORY_SNAPSHOT_PROVIDER is indexed as text, and nothing else changes: any other provider string, and any snapshot frame whose bytes are not valid UTF-8, returns Ok(None) so the projection still advances its checkpoint with an empty mutation set instead of failing. The existing rule-based extractor already produces exactly the aliases a code fact carries — paths, urls, hex ids, structured ids and proper nouns (crates/hm-index/src/entity_rules.rs:21) — so file paths and symbol names become postings without any new extraction rule."
do_2 = "The lexical BM25 projection is deliberately left alone: activation can only decode message kinds into bundle items (crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs:669), so indexing snapshot shards lexically would put undecodable candidates into the manifest. The consumer is g03-t5, whose test recalls an ingested snapshot by entity."
do_3 = "Prove it: A ProviderFrame frame whose provider is the repository snapshot carrier and whose content holds two fact lines is indexed: EntityProjection::query for a path that appears in the content returns that frame's LSN. No other projection, no key layout and no ProjectionId changes; cargo test -p hm-proj --test entities passes and the pre-existing --test lexical and --test rebuild suites still pass."

[task.3.5]
title = "remember gains a repository-snapshot surface"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "surface"
requires = ["3.3", "3.4"]
reqs = ["3.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/repository_snapshot.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_snapshot"
do_1 = "Add RememberKind::RepositorySnapshot to the existing remember verb so a caller can hand the engine a repository snapshot document it produced itself. The verb appends the document as externally observed ProviderFrame events whose provider is the pinned carrier string, chunked on line boundaries so every shard holds whole facts and a fact's byte range never straddles two events; a single line larger than the chunk size, or a document needing more than 256 shards, is refused with CapacityExceeded rather than truncated. Embeddings are not requested for this kind: a snapshot shard is structured evidence, not prose, and embedding it would spend a provider call on JSON. The envelope reports the shard count and the snapshot digest so the caller can name the same snapshot later."
do_2 = "Finally, event_content learns to render a snapshot ProviderFrame as its UTF-8 text, so the entity recall path from g03-t4 returns readable content instead of an empty string. The engine still starts no process and downloads nothing: this is an append of caller-supplied bytes."
do_3 = "Prove it: remember with kind: 'repository_snapshot' appends N ProviderFrame events with Authority::ExternalObserved and provider == hm_schema::event::REPOSITORY_SNAPSHOT_PROVIDER, each verifying at Boundary::Disk. cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_snapshot passes and the pre-existing --test tools suite still passes."

[task.3.6]
title = "Actor read commands for graph neighbourhoods and visible memories"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "surface"
requires = []
reqs = ["3.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/graph.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --test graph"
do_1 = "The graph and memories projections are written by consolidation runs but the daemon exposes no way to read them: ActorEngine has per-projection accessors for intentions, predictions, procedures and attention, and nothing for edges or memory records. Add two commands in the same shape (crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs:620 is the template): one returns the visible memory records of the active generation, the other returns a node's neighbourhood — the node's own memory record, the edges touching it that are valid at the requested instant, and, for each edge, the memory record of the other endpoint, all read from one snapshot so a neighbourhood is internally consistent. Both resolve the generation through RunsProjection::active_generation and go through the generation-aware readers, so retracted and unpublished generations stay invisible exactly as GraphProjection::neighbours and MemoryProjection::get_visible already enforce."
do_2 = "Arguments are bounded: an empty node id or a zero or over-256 limit is InvalidArgument. These two commands are the read half that g03-t7 needs for mint-versus-revise and that g03-t8 turns into a recall surface."
do_3 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::graph_neighbourhood(node_id, valid_at_ns, limit) on an actor holding a published generation with two memories and one edge returns generation equal to the active generation, node equal to the anchor's memory record, and one neighbour whose edge.relation and endpoint.name are the expected values, with outgoing == true when the anchor is the edge source. cargo test -p hm-serve --test graph passes and the pre-existing --test actor suite still passes."

[task.3.7]
title = "Repository extraction run inside the consolidate verb"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "surface"
requires = ["3.1", "3.2", "3.3", "3.5", "3.6"]
reqs = ["3.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/repository.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/repository_extract.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_extract"
do_1 = "Add ConsolidateMode::Repository, a background, budgeted, generation-scoped run that derives a repository graph from an already-ingested snapshot with no model call at all. The run finds the newest complete snapshot in the repository's conversation, parses and resolves it with hm_cortex::repograph, and stages one derived event per node and per edge under a run id that names the snapshot digest: a node absent from the active generation's visible memories is minted, a node already present is revised against its current version, and every edge is asserted with its evidence-counted weight. Every derived event carries Authority::DerivedInference, the pinned deterministic extraction provenance with zero tokens and zero cost, and a citation naming the exact byte range of the snapshot line it came from."
do_2 = "The run opens with ConsolidationOpened (single Publish phase, one contract entry in prompts, the declared budget), stages in batches of at most 200 events so the protocol batch limit is respected, and closes with ConsolidationClosed, which is the compare-and-swap that publishes the generation. Re-running the same snapshot for the same repository is detected as a duplicate through the existing run history and changes nothing. The run never constructs a provider: a missing snapshot is OperationUnavailable, a malformed one is SchemaInvalid, and no LLM runtime is consulted on any path."
do_3 = "Prove it: consolidate with action: 'run', mode: 'repository', scope: '<repository>' on an actor whose snapshot was ingested by the repository-snapshot remember surface publishes a generation and returns an envelope naming repository, snapshot_digest, shards, facts, skipped, nodes, edges, dropped, generation, parent_generation and run_id. cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_extract passes and the pre-existing --test sleep suite still passes."

[task.3.8]
title = "recall gains a graph mode over the repository graph"
status = "done"
wave = 3
owner_lane = "integration"
requires = ["3.6", "3.7"]
reqs = ["3.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/graph.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/recall.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/repository_graph.rs", "docs/concepts/repository-graph.md", "docs/SUMMARY.md", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_graph"
do_1 = "Close the slice with the read surface the acceptance criteria already name: recall gains the graph mode, which walks the validated edges of the published generation from an anchor node. The anchor is either an explicit node id in hex, as returned by the extraction run and by the mode's own items, or a repository name plus a node name, which the surface resolves by computing the candidate node id for each of the six fact kinds and taking the one that has a visible memory record. Each item names the relation, the direction, the endpoint node id and name, the evidence-counted weight, the validity interval and the asserting event, and carries derived_inference authority plus the provenance URIs of the edge event and its cited snapshot lines, so a caller can always walk back from a graph answer to the observed bytes."
do_2 = "An anchor that resolves to nothing returns an ok envelope with an explicit gap rather than silence, because silent degradation is a tested bug class here. The end-to-end test runs the whole slice on one real actor: ingest a snapshot, extract it, traverse it, restart the actor, traverse again. The docs page states plainly that the engine reads a snapshot the caller produced and never runs or installs a producer."
do_3 = "Prove it: recall with mode: 'graph' and filters.anchor set to a 64-character node id hex returns one item per neighbouring edge, each with relation, direction, node_id, name, weight_micros, valid_from_ns, valid_to_ns, edge_lsn, authority: 'derived_inference' and a hm://<actor>/lsn/<edge_lsn> uri. cargo test -p hm-mcp --test repository_graph passes and the pre-existing --test tools suite still passes."

[task.4.1]
title = "Response outcome vocabulary and classification on the OpenAI-compatible provider"
status = "done"
wave = 4
section = "Wave 4 - Provider honesty: response outcomes, extraction contracts and run reservations"
owner_lane = "l3"
requires = []
reqs = ["4.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-llm/src/outcome.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/openai_compat.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs", "crates/hm-llm/tests/outcomes.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-llm --locked"
do_1 = "Give hm-llm a single, versioned vocabulary for what a provider actually returned, so a refusal, a truncation, unparseable text and a structurally incomplete answer stop collapsing into the same Wire/Schema string. Add crates/hm-llm/src/outcome.rs with ResponseOutcome (Refused, Truncated, Malformed, Incomplete), ResponseFault (version, outcome, model_id, detail, requested_output_tokens, usage) and a shared decode_structured_text helper that turns the model's returned text into a serde_json::Value or the right fault. Add one variant LlmError::Response(ResponseFault) and wire the classification into OpenAiCompatible::generate_structured in this strict order: refusal first, then truncation, then content decode, leaving the existing strict usage extraction and with_cost accounting exactly as they are."
do_2 = "A fault carries the usage the provider reported for the failed attempt so a later caller can charge it honestly rather than pretending nothing was spent. Update the one exhaustive match over LlmError outside the crate, in the MCP reconstruct tool, so the workspace still compiles and each outcome reaches a distinct-or-documented error code. The three remaining providers are classified in g04-t2 and the envelope surface lands in g04-t3."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_llm::outcome::RESPONSE_CONTRACT_VERSION is 1 and every ResponseFault constructed by ResponseFault::new carries it in its version field. crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs maps LlmError::Response by outcome: Refused -> ErrorCode::OperationUnavailable, Truncated -> ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded, Malformed and Incomplete -> ErrorCode::SchemaInvalid."

[task.4.2]
title = "Classify refused, truncated, malformed and incomplete responses on the remaining three providers"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l3"
requires = ["4.1"]
reqs = ["4.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-llm/src/anthropic.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/gemini.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/ollama.rs", "crates/hm-llm/tests/outcomes.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-llm --locked"
do_1 = "Extend the response-outcome classification from g04-t1 to the Anthropic, Gemini and Ollama providers so the vocabulary is provider-independent and a HyperMind deployment cannot lose the distinction by changing provider. Each provider keeps its own body shape: Anthropic signals both refusal and truncation through the top-level stop_reason, Gemini through /candidates/0/finishReason plus /promptFeedback/blockReason, and Ollama only through /done_reason because it has no refusal channel. Anthropic returns the structured result as a JSON object rather than text, so it cannot be malformed — an absent tool result is Incomplete."
do_2 = "Each provider gains a small best-effort usage reader used only to fill a fault; Ollama's already-tolerant usage handling is unchanged, and Anthropic's and Gemini's strict success-path usage extraction stays exactly as it is. No shared helper is refactored and no existing fixture file is edited on disk."
do_3 = "Prove it: Anthropic: a body with 'stop_reason': 'refusal' yields ResponseOutcome::Refused; 'stop_reason': 'max_tokens' yields ResponseOutcome::Truncated; a body with neither and no tool_use item carrying input yields ResponseOutcome::Incomplete instead of the previous LlmError::Wire. The four existing tests in crates/hm-llm/tests/providers.rs pass unchanged, including the 18 microUSD cost assertions for all three providers."

[task.4.3]
title = "Surface the response outcome as a typed gap on recall in reconstruct mode"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["4.1"]
reqs = ["4.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/reconstruction_surface.rs", "docs/reference/mcp.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test reconstruction_surface --locked"
do_1 = "Make the four outcomes diagnosable from outside the process without adding a verb or an error code. Today a provider failure inside recall in Reconstruct mode collapses into a bare error envelope whose code cannot tell a refusal from unparseable text."
do_2 = "Change crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs::run so that a LlmError::Response(fault) returns an envelope that is still ok: false and still carries the mapped ErrorCode, but also carries one gaps entry of kind extraction_outcome naming the outcome, the contract id, the version, the detail, the model id, the requested output budget and the observed output tokens, plus a warnings line extraction_outcome:<outcome>. Every other LlmError keeps returning Err(Error) exactly as before. The envelope stays inside the fourteen-verb inventory and no new argument is accepted."
do_3 = "Prove it: A reconstruct call whose recorded provider response is a refusal returns an envelope with ok == false, items[0]['error'] == 'kOperationUnavailable', exactly one gaps entry with kind == 'extraction_outcome' and outcome == 'refused', and a warning equal to extraction_outcome:refused. No new MCP verb, no new tool argument, no ErrorCode variant, and no change to crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs, so the docs tool catalog is unchanged."

[task.4.4]
title = "Typed extraction contract with bounded identifiers in hm-llm"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l3"
requires = ["4.1"]
reqs = ["4.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-llm/src/contract.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-llm/tests/contracts.rs", "crates/hm-llm/Cargo.toml", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-llm --test contracts --locked"
do_1 = "Give HyperMind a declarative, versioned way to state the exact shape a structured-output response must have, checked on the raw JSON before anything downstream trusts it. Add crates/hm-llm/src/contract.rs with ExtractionContract (contract_id, version, a static slice of FieldRule), FieldShape (Identifier, NullableIdentifier, Prose, IdentifierList, Count, Flag, Opaque) and ContractViolation. Validation is exact in both directions: every declared field must be present and every present key must be declared, so a model that invents a field or drops one is refused rather than silently trimmed."
do_2 = "Identifiers are bounded in characters rather than bytes so the same bound means the same thing in every script, and the bound sits below the ledger's own identifier ceiling so a value that passes here can never be rejected later for length. Prose and list fields get their own separate bounds because a definition is not a label. A violation converts into a ResponseFault with outcome Incomplete, reusing the g04-t1 vocabulary, and its diagnostic text names the field and the observed length but never the value."
do_3 = "The first consumer is g04-t5 in the same group."
do_4 = "Prove it: EXTRACTION_CONTRACT_VERSION is 1, MAXIMUM_IDENTIFIER_CHARACTERS is 512, MAXIMUM_PROSE_CHARACTERS is 65_536 and MAXIMUM_LIST_ITEMS is 64, and all four are pub const with no configuration path. ExtractionContract::fault produces a ResponseFault with outcome == ResponseOutcome::Incomplete, version == RESPONSE_CONTRACT_VERSION and detail == violation.detail()."

[task.4.5]
title = "Validate the NREM merge response against its extraction contract before a derived event is staged"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = ["4.4"]
reqs = ["4.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/nrem.rs", "docs/concepts/consolidation.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test nrem --locked"
do_1 = "Put the typed extraction contract in front of the only structured-output step whose result becomes a ledger record today. crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs currently parses the merge response with permissive accessors and collapses every structural problem into DropReason::InvalidStructuredOutput, so an oversized memory name would travel all the way to event admission before anything noticed. Declare merge_contract() describing the seven fields of the merge-cluster response, run it as the first step of validate_response, and drop the candidate with a new DropReason::ExtractionContract(ContractViolation) naming the exact field when it fails."
do_2 = "The existing citation, thought-quality, rewrite-guard and mint-independence gates are untouched and still run afterwards. Because a contract failure lands in NremReport.dropped, the existing consolidation staging loop already refuses to mint from it and already counts it into ConsolidationPhase.dropped_candidates, so no derived event can be created from a response that failed the contract."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_cortex::nrem::merge::merge_contract() is a pub const fn returning an ExtractionContract with contract_id == 'merge-cluster@1', version == hm_llm::contract::EXTRACTION_CONTRACT_VERSION, and exactly seven rules: action Identifier, target NullableIdentifier, name Identifier, definition Prose, tags IdentifierList, salience_micros Count, citations Opaque. The existing crates/hm-cortex/tests/nrem.rs tests pass unchanged, including the three-cluster report assertions (llm_calls == 3, one Mint decision, citation_invalid == 1, a Citation drop and a SpeculationPoisoned drop) and the ported quality regression vectors."

[task.4.6]
title = "Run reservations over the declared consolidation budget"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = []
reqs = ["4.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/budget.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/reservation.rs", "docs/concepts/consolidation.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test reservation --locked"
do_1 = "Today a consolidation run charges its budget after the provider answers, so nothing can decide in advance whether a further attempt is affordable and a retry would be a pure overrun. Extend crates/hm-cortex/src/budget.rs with RunReservation, which holds the run's ConsolidationBudget, the settled BudgetUsage and the outstanding reservations, and admits an attempt only when settled plus outstanding plus the request still fits. Reserve the two dimensions knowable before a call: one llm call, and the request's maximum_output_tokens as an upper bound on the output it can produce."
do_2 = "Settle with the real hm_llm::Usage afterwards, including the usage of an attempt that failed, so a refusal or a truncation is charged rather than forgiven. Release exists for the case where no tokens were spent at all, such as a transport error before the request left. Wall time deliberately stays with the existing BudgetTracker; the reservation covers calls, tokens and cost only, and RunReservation never mutates state on a refusal so an aborted phase still reports its last good usage."
do_3 = "The consumer is g04-t7."
do_4 = "Prove it: RunReservation::new(limits) starts with zero settled usage and zero outstanding reservation, and settled() returns BudgetUsage::default(). A ReservationTicket is #[must_use] and carries no public fields, so it cannot be forged or reused after settling."

[task.4.7]
title = "Reserved single re-ask for repairable provider outcomes in the NREM merge loop"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = ["4.2", "4.5", "4.6"]
reqs = ["4.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/nrem.rs", "docs/concepts/consolidation.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test nrem --locked"
do_1 = "Turn the classified outcomes into a bounded repair path that cannot outspend the run. Add MergeOptions and consolidate_clusters_reserved to crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs: per cluster, reserve a call and its output ceiling through RunReservation, send the request, settle the real usage, and on a classified fault decide whether one re-ask is warranted. A refusal is never re-asked — asking the same question again does not repair a decision to decline."
do_2 = "A truncation is re-asked once at the raised retry_output_tokens ceiling, and that raised ceiling is what gets reserved, so a retry can never step outside the declared budget. A malformed or incomplete response is re-asked once at the same ceiling. When the reservation refuses the next attempt the cluster is dropped and counted rather than the run overrunning."
do_3 = "Keep the existing consolidate_clusters signature and have it delegate with an unbounded reservation and a single attempt, so every existing caller, fixture and eval suite behaves exactly as before. Report the extra attempts so the surface can show them."
do_4 = "Prove it: consolidate_clusters(provider, run_id, clusters, existing) keeps its current signature and delegates to consolidate_clusters_reserved with RunReservation::unbounded() and MergeOptions { maximum_attempts_per_cluster: 1, retry_output_tokens: MERGE_OUTPUT_TOKENS }, and all existing hm-cortex, hm-eval and hm-sim merge tests pass unchanged. A truncation re-ask whose retry_output_tokens is not greater than the ceiling that already truncated is not attempted; the cluster is dropped with DropReason::ProviderOutcome(ResponseOutcome::Truncated)."

[task.4.8]
title = "Drive the consolidation run through the reservation and report it in the consolidate envelope"
status = "done"
wave = 4
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["4.7"]
reqs = ["4.3", "4.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/consolidation_outcomes.rs", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/concepts/consolidation.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test consolidation_outcomes --locked"
do_1 = "Close the vertical: make the real consolidation run use the reserved merge ladder and make the result visible on the surface, end to end through MCP, the actor and the ledger. In crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs, build a RunReservation from the run's declared ConsolidationBudget and call consolidate_clusters_reserved instead of consolidate_clusters, with MergeOptions derived from the declared budget so the retry ceiling is a property of the run rather than a hidden constant. Keep the existing post-phase budget check and the existing CapacityExceeded abort, so a genuine overrun still fails the phase."
do_2 = "Populate the previously unused budget field of the consolidate envelope with the declared limits, the settled usage and the retry count, all versioned. Prove the whole path with a test that drives the consolidate verb against a recorded provider: a truncated first answer repaired on the second attempt mints exactly one MemoryMinted event in the ledger, and the same run under a one-call budget mints nothing and counts the candidate as dropped."
do_3 = "Prove it: The NREM branch builds RunReservation::new(budget.into()) once per run and passes it to consolidate_clusters_reserved; the cluster truncation by budget.max_llm_calls stays in place as a coarse pre-filter. crates/hm-mcp/tests/sleep.rs and crates/hm-sim/tests/slice6_journey.rs pass unchanged."

[task.5.1]
title = "VocabularyImported ledger event: schema v2 union member, validation, ledger kind and authority"
status = "done"
wave = 5
section = "Wave 5 - Vocabulary: imported terms, reviewed aliases and alias-aware graph recall"
owner_lane = "schema"
requires = []
reqs = ["5.1"]
touches = ["schemas/events.fbs", "crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs", "crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/src/frame.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/checkpoint.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/authority.rs", "crates/hm-schema/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/reference/generated/schema-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-schema --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Add one additive schema-v2 event kind that records a versioned, source-backed vocabulary import so the rest of the group has a real ledger record to project from. In schemas/events.fbs declare enum VocabularyCategory : ubyte { entity_type, entity_instance, relation }, table VocabularyTerm { term_id:string (required); canonical_name:string (required); category:VocabularyCategory; parent_term_id:string; aliases:[string]; } and table VocabularyImported { vocabulary_id:[ubyte] (required); version:ushort; source_uri:string (required); source_media_type:string (required); source_digest:[ubyte] (required); terms:[VocabularyTerm] (required); ignored_triples:uint; }, then append VocabularyImported as the LAST member of union EventPayload (union order is the persisted discriminant). Regenerate crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs with planus and hand-edit nothing in it."
do_2 = "Wire the kind through crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs: discriminant 44, the TryFrom<u8> arm, membership in is_wave_seven (a kind outside every wave can never verify, event.rs:316), the payload_kind arm, a validate_payload arm calling a new validate_vocabulary_imported, and an authority guard in validate_envelope that rejects any envelope whose authority is not Authority::UserAsserted with ErrorCode::ProtectedTypeWrite. Mirror the discriminant in crates/hm-ledger/src/frame.rs (enum plus const KINDS: [EventKind; 44]), add the ledger-to-schema row in crates/hm-proj/src/checkpoint.rs schema_kind, and add the arm in crates/hm-cortex/src/authority.rs authority_for_event returning Authority::UserAsserted. The consumers are g05-t3 (projection) and g05-t5 (importer), both ordered after this task."
do_3 = "Prove it: schemas/events.fbs declares VocabularyCategory, VocabularyTerm and VocabularyImported, and VocabularyImported is the last name in union EventPayload; no existing union member moved. No existing test in crates/hm-schema, crates/hm-ledger, crates/hm-proj or crates/hm-cortex changes behaviour."

[task.5.2]
title = "Unicode-aware vocabulary name normalization and thresholded Q16 alias suggestions in hm-index"
status = "done"
wave = 5
owner_lane = "index"
requires = []
reqs = ["5.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-index/src/vocabulary.rs", "crates/hm-index/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-index/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-index --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Add crates/hm-index/src/vocabulary.rs, the single home for vocabulary name normalization and fuzzy alias suggestion, with no new third-party dependency and no floating point. normalize_name lowercases with Rust's Unicode-aware str::to_lowercase, replaces every character where char::is_alphanumeric() is false with '_', collapses runs of '_', trims leading and trailing '_', and is idempotent; this is deliberately wider than the ASCII-only splitter used by the graph lane today (crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/graph.rs terms()), so accented and non-Latin names survive. normalized_segments splits a phrase into its normalized alphanumeric segments, sorted, deduped and truncated. similarity_q16 scores two names by Q16 fixed-point Dice overlap of their DISTINCT adjacent character-pair sets, computed over Unicode scalar values so a multi-byte character costs exactly one position, with u64 intermediates and truncating division. suggest_aliases returns every candidate at or above a caller-supplied threshold, ordered by descending similarity then ascending candidate, and never selects a winner: it is a review list, not a merge. All inputs are bounded and every out-of-range argument returns hm_core::Error with ErrorCode::InvalidArgument. Consumers are g05-t3 (projection alias keys), g05-t4 (graph lane) and g05-t7 (review surface), all ordered after this task."
do_2 = "Prove it: normalize_name('Works For') == 'works_for', normalize_name('works_for') == 'works_for' (idempotent), normalize_name(' --Café Client-- ') == 'café_client', normalize_name('ÄÖÜ') == 'äöü', normalize_name('---') == ''. suggest_aliases returns Err(ErrorCode::InvalidArgument) for limit == 0, for threshold_q16 == 0, for threshold_q16 > Q16_ONE, and for more than MAXIMUM_CANDIDATES candidates."

[task.5.3]
title = "Vocabulary projection: versioned head, term records and exact alias postings rebuilt from the ledger"
status = "done"
wave = 5
owner_lane = "projections"
requires = ["5.1", "5.2"]
reqs = ["5.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/store.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/vocabulary.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/rebuild.rs", "crates/hm-proj/Cargo.toml", "crates/hm-proj/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Add ProjectionId::Vocabulary as the nineteenth projection and crates/hm-proj/src/vocabulary.rs, a simple (non-generation-scoped) projection modelled end to end on crates/hm-proj/src/attestations.rs. apply_event ignores every kind except hm_ledger::frame::EventKind::VocabularyImported by applying an empty mutation set so the checkpoint still advances, verifies the frame with crate::checkpoint::verify_frame, and refuses a payload that is not EventPayload::VocabularyImported with ErrorCode::InvalidKind. Version supersession is the projection's rule: if a head record already exists for this vocabulary_id with a version greater than or equal to the incoming version, the import is recorded as seen with an empty mutation set and changes nothing; otherwise the head record is replaced and one term record per term is written under a key that includes the version, so definitions are never overwritten in place. Alias postings map a normalized name to the terms that declare it: for every term, hm_index::vocabulary::normalize_name is applied to the canonical_name and to each alias, and the resulting AliasEntry is merged into a sorted, deduplicated posting list."
do_2 = "All keys are fixed-size 33-byte blake3 digests so no key can exceed the LMDB key bound. The read API serves g05-t4 (graph lane) and g05-t7 (review surface), both ordered after this task. Follow the crate rules exactly: open the snapshot, build mutations, drop(snapshot) before store.apply, never hold a read transaction across a write."
do_3 = "Prove it: ProjectionId gains a Vocabulary variant appended last, PROJECTION_NAMES gains 'vocabulary' at the same index, and ProjectionId::COUNT == 19; ProjectionId::Vocabulary.name() == 'vocabulary'. terms(snapshot, limit) returns head-version terms across all vocabularies sorted by (vocabulary_id, term_id); vocabulary, list, terms and resolve all reject limit == 0 with ErrorCode::InvalidArgument."

[task.5.4]
title = "Alias-aware relation gating in the graph recall lane"
status = "done"
wave = 5
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["5.3"]
reqs = ["5.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/graph.rs", "crates/hm-compose/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Make the graph lane reach neighbours whose edge relation is named differently from the query but is the same reviewed vocabulary relation. crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/graph.rs today drops any edge whose relation shares no literal ASCII token with the query (relation_overlap == 0), so an edge relation of 'works_for' is invisible to the query 'employs'. Add a second, additive overlap source: resolve both the query string and each edge relation string to vocabulary relation term ids through hm_proj::vocabulary::VocabularyProjection::resolve on the ReadSnapshot the lane already holds, keeping only terms whose category is VocabularyCategory::Relation, and add the size of the intersection to the existing literal overlap. The gate itself is unchanged: an edge with zero total overlap is still skipped, so the lane never widens beyond real edges and never invents a candidate. Only exact normalized names resolve; hm_index::vocabulary::suggest_aliases is deliberately not called from the lane, so an unreviewed fuzzy resemblance can never change retrieval."
do_2 = "Bound the work with MAXIMUM_VOCABULARY_TERMS = 64 resolved terms per string and a per-search BTreeMap cache keyed by the relation string so each distinct relation is resolved once per search. The public search signature does not change, so no caller in hm-mcp, hm-serve or hm-sim is touched."
do_3 = "Prove it: graph::search returns the neighbour reached by an edge whose relation is 'works_for' when the query is 'employs' and a vocabulary declares a Relation term whose canonical_name is 'works_for' with alias 'employs'. graph::search keeps its existing signature and MAXIMUM_VISITED_NODES semantics; no new pub type, RetrievalLane variant, WhyCode variant, GapKind or canonical HMA1 byte is added."

[task.5.5]
title = "Vocabulary source reader: bounded N-Triples parsing into a digest-bound import envelope"
status = "done"
wave = 5
owner_lane = "cognition"
requires = ["5.1"]
reqs = ["5.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/vocabulary.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/ingest.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Add crates/hm-cortex/src/vocabulary.rs, the deterministic reader that turns an RDF source document into one VocabularyImported envelope, with no new third-party dependency. parse_terms accepts line-based RDF triples (N-Triples): a line is blank, a comment starting with '#', or <subject-iri> <predicate-iri> object . where object is <iri> or a quoted literal with an optional @language or ^^<datatype> suffix that is read and discarded; anything else is rejected with ErrorCode::SchemaInvalid so a document is never half-imported silently. Recognised predicates build the term set: rdf:type with object owl:Class or rdfs:Class yields category EntityType, with owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty or rdf:Property yields Relation, with owl:NamedIndividual yields EntityInstance; rdfs:label and skos:altLabel literals become aliases; owl:equivalentClass, owl:equivalentProperty and owl:sameAs IRIs contribute the object's local name as an alias; rdfs:subClassOf and rdfs:subPropertyOf set parent_term_id. Every other triple increments ignored_triples. term_id is the full subject IRI, canonical_name is its local name after the last '#' or '/'; a subject with no recognised rdf:type is not a term."
do_2 = "Output is sorted by term_id with aliases sorted and deduplicated so the same document always produces the same bytes. import_envelope hashes the source bytes with blake3 into source_digest, sets source_media_type to 'application/n-triples', and runs the envelope through crate::ingest::ingest with IngestSource::User so authority comes from the source kind exactly like every other ingested event. The consumer is g05-t6, ordered after this task."
do_3 = "Prove it: parse_terms over a fixture document declaring one owl:Class with an rdfs:label, one owl:ObjectProperty with an rdfs:label, a skos:altLabel and an owl:equivalentProperty, one owl:NamedIndividual, one rdfs:subPropertyOf and two unrecognised triples returns exactly three terms sorted by term_id, with the expected categories, canonical names, parent_term_id and sorted deduplicated aliases, and an ignored_triples count of exactly 2. crate::ingest::ingest gains an IngestSource::User arm for EventKind::VocabularyImported; every other ingest behaviour is unchanged and crates/hm-cortex/tests/authority.rs still passes."

[task.5.6]
title = "Vocabulary import through the existing remember verb"
status = "done"
wave = 5
owner_lane = "surface"
requires = ["5.3", "5.5"]
reqs = ["5.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/vocabulary.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test vocabulary"
do_1 = "Give operators a way to import a versioned vocabulary without adding an MCP verb: extend the existing remember verb with RememberKind::Vocabulary. Add a VocabularyInput { vocabulary_id, version, source_uri } to crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs and an optional vocabulary field on RememberInput. In crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs remember_inner, after the existing empty-argument checks, the reconstruct::guard_remember call and the Retention::DoNotStore receipt path, branch on RememberKind::Vocabulary before the chunking path: require the vocabulary block (ErrorCode::InvalidArgument when absent, when vocabulary_id is empty or longer than 4096 bytes, or when version is 0), call hm_cortex::vocabulary::import_envelope with the tool content as the source document, and append exactly one IncomingEvent with kind hm_ledger::frame::EventKind::VocabularyImported."
do_2 = "Vocabulary imports never take the embedding path and never chunk: one document is one versioned event. The response envelope reports first_lsn, vocabulary_id, version, source_uri, source_media_type, source_digest, term_count and ignored_triples, pushes the single hm:// provenance URI, and carries a warning stating that an import declares a vocabulary and does not merge any existing identity. The dispatcher, protocol verb allowlist, REST VERBS and OpenAPI are untouched because tool arguments are opaque JSON end to end."
do_3 = "Prove it: A remember call with kind 'vocabulary', a valid N-Triples content document and a vocabulary block appends exactly one ledger event and returns ok with items[0] carrying first_lsn, vocabulary_id, version, source_uri, source_media_type 'application/n-triples', a 64-character hex source_digest, term_count and ignored_triples. The MCP verb inventory is still exactly fourteen: crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs, the #[tool] router in crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs, hm_schema::protocol's ToolRequest allowlist and hm_serve::rest::VERBS are unchanged."

[task.5.7]
title = "Reviewable alias proposals through the existing inspect verb"
