verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test vocabulary_review"
do_1 = "Close the loop on item 12 by making fuzzy alias matching a reviewable read, never a write. Add VocabularyProjection::suggest to crates/hm-proj/src/vocabulary.rs: it reads head-version term records, builds the candidate set from each term's normalized canonical_name and normalized aliases, scores the observed name with hm_index::vocabulary::suggest_aliases at a caller-supplied threshold, and returns AliasProposal rows carrying the vocabulary, version, term id, canonical name, category, matched candidate and similarity_q16. Expose it through the actor with two ActorEngine commands and two async methods, following the AttentionHistory and Calibration pattern exactly."
do_2 = "Surface both reads inside the existing inspect verb: hm://{actor}/vocabulary lists the imported vocabularies with their version, source uri, source media type, source digest and term count plus one provenance URI per import event, and hm://{actor}/vocabulary/aliases?name=<observed>[&threshold_q16=<n>] returns the thresholded proposal list. Every proposal is reported with accepted false and the envelope carries a warning stating that a proposal changes nothing and is accepted only by importing a new vocabulary version that declares the alias. No event is written by either read, and no proposal can affect the graph lane, which resolves only exact reviewed names."
do_3 = "Prove it: VocabularyProjection::suggest returns proposals sorted by descending similarity_q16 then ascending (vocabulary_id, term_id), truncated to limit, and rejects limit == 0, threshold_q16 == 0 and threshold_q16 > Q16_ONE with ErrorCode::InvalidArgument. inspect's existing hm://{actor}/attention, hm://{actor}/calibration and hm://{actor}/lsn/{n} branches are unchanged and crates/hm-mcp/tests/tools.rs still passes."

[task.6.1]
title = "Deterministic relationship representations with edge and source provenance"
status = "done"
wave = 6
section = "Wave 6 - Relationships: a relation lane, paired evidence and support provenance"
owner_lane = "cognition"
requires = []
reqs = ["6.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/relations.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/relations.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test relations"
do_1 = "Add a pure, LLM-free builder in hm-cortex that turns validated graph relationships into the deterministic text a relationship embedding is built from, together with the edge identity and the source LSNs that produced the relationship. The builder takes plain relationship inputs (edge id, the LSN of the asserting event, both endpoint ids, the relation phrase and the citation LSNs) and returns one representation per distinct relationship, each carrying a stable relation key, the asserting event LSN, the rendered text and the sorted support LSNs. It refuses unusable inputs with a typed drop reason rather than silently skipping them, mirroring how NREM records DroppedCandidate (crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs:49-66)."
do_2 = "Duplicate relationships collapse to the latest assertion so a re-asserted edge does not produce two embeddings. Bounds are explicit: a maximum relationship count and a maximum text length, both rejected as InvalidArgument when nonsensical, with CapacityExceeded above 4096 inputs. The module makes no ledger, projection, provider or LLM call; it is the reference function that later tasks in this group drive from the background run."
do_3 = "Follow the smallest complete cortex module shape (crates/hm-cortex/src/rem/abstract.rs) for module layout and typed error enums."
do_4 = "Prove it: crates/hm-cortex/src/relations.rs exists, is declared in crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs in alphabetical position between quality and rem, and contains no LLM, network or filesystem call. Output is sorted by edge_lsn ascending and truncated to maximum_relations; truncation does not add a drop entry."

[task.6.2]
title = "Graph projection reads for relationships by event LSN and by generation"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "projections"
requires = []
reqs = ["6.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/graph.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/graph.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --test graph"
do_1 = "The graph projection can currently only be walked from a node (GraphProjection::neighbours, crates/hm-proj/src/graph.rs:144), which is not enough to enumerate relationships for background embedding or to resolve a relationship hit back to its edge. Add two read primitives on GraphProjection: one that returns the EdgeRecord stored at a given asserting event LSN, and one that lists the relationships visible in a generation's published lineage, retraction-filtered and validity-filtered, in deterministic order. Both read through a ReadSnapshot only and write nothing; follow the existing private helpers (edge_key at graph.rs:232, read_edge at graph.rs:187, is_retracted at graph.rs:194, valid_at at graph.rs:205, RunsProjection::lineage)."
do_2 = "The listing gates on RunsProjection::is_readable exactly like MemoryProjection::list_visible (crates/hm-proj/src/memories.rs:221-245) so an open generation is never readable, and dedupes by edge_id across the lineage so the newest published generation wins. Add a head-prefix helper mirroring memories.rs's head_generation_prefix. No projection id, no rebuild wiring and no new event kind: this is read-only surface on an existing projection."
do_3 = "Prove it: GraphProjection::edge_at(snapshot, event_lsn) returns Some(EdgeRecord) for an asserted edge's event LSN, None for an LSN with no edge record, and ErrorCode::InvalidArgument for event_lsn == 0. Neither function writes: crates/hm-proj/tests/graph.rs asserts snapshot.canonical_dump(ProjectionId::Graph) is byte-identical before and after both calls."

[task.6.3]
title = "Background relationship embeddings appended after a consolidation publish"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["6.1", "6.2"]
reqs = ["6.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/relation.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/relations.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test relations"
do_1 = "Build relationship embeddings in the background, as part of the existing consolidate verb, never on a recall path. Give ActorEngine a read command that returns the relationships visible in the active generation, resolved through GraphProjection::list_edges at the actor's own monotonic wall clock. Add an hm-mcp module that turns those relationships into representations with hm_cortex::relations::represent, skips relationships that already carry an embedding in the relation space, embeds the remainder through the existing EmbeddingRuntime, and appends one EventPayload::Embedding per relationship whose target_lsn is the LSN of the asserting EdgeAsserted event and whose space_id is the relation space."
do_2 = "The build runs after a consolidate run has published, is bounded by an explicit relationship cap, and can never fail the run: a build error becomes a gap plus a warning on the envelope, exactly like the document-embedding failure path in crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs:325-334. No new MCP verb: this is a surface inside the frozen consolidate verb."
do_3 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::relations(limit) returns the EdgeRecords of the active generation, filtered by the actor's own last wall timestamp, and ErrorCode::InvalidArgument for limit == 0. An embedding failure leaves the published run intact and adds a gap {'kind':'relation_embedding_pending'} plus one warning, with envelope.ok still true."

[task.6.4]
title = "Relation retrieval lane in hm-compose with its own lane and why codes"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["6.2"]
reqs = ["6.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/relation.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/mod.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/fusion.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/planner.rs", "crates/hm-compose/tests/relation_lane.rs", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test relation_lane"
do_1 = "Add the relation lane to hm-compose so relationship ranking lives where every other lane's ranking lives. The lane is a pure function: it takes the vector hits produced against the relation embedding lane together with the EdgeRecords those hits resolve to, and returns a LaneRanking on RetrievalLane::Relation whose candidates are keyed by edge id, carry the asserting event LSN, and take their salience from the edge weight. Hits with no resolved edge, a zero LSN or an empty edge id are dropped; fusion's own guards (crates/hm-compose/src/fusion.rs:65-73) reject anything else, so salience is clamped with .max(1) exactly as the graph lane does (crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/graph.rs:108)."
do_2 = "Append RetrievalLane::Relation and WhyCode::Relation to their enums, extend the three exhaustive matches that will otherwise fail to compile (fusion::lane_name, fusion::why_name, bundle::provenance_uri), give why_code a single-lane arm for Relation, and add the planner arm so a relation-mode plan selects the lane. The graph lane, which today gates purely on relation-term overlap, is left untouched; the relation lane is the semantic complement to it."
do_3 = "Prove it: crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/relation.rs exists, is registered in crates/hm-compose/src/lanes/mod.rs alphabetically, and reads no snapshot: it is a pure function over hits and records. The existing ten-section HMA1 assertions still pass: cargo test -p hm-compose --test bundle is green."

[task.6.5]
title = "Relation recall mode that separates relationship support from included text"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["6.3", "6.4"]
reqs = ["6.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/recall.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/relations.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test relations"
do_1 = "Make relationships retrievable through the existing recall verb. Add a relation request to the daemon's recall dispatch that embeds nothing itself: it takes the relation-space query vector and prefilter, searches the relation VectorLane, resolves every hit's target LSN to an EdgeRecord with GraphProjection::edge_at, drops retracted or out-of-validity edges, ranks them through hm_compose::lanes::relation::rank, and returns a typed relationship result carrying the edge identity, the relation phrase, both endpoints, the asserting event LSN and the citation LSNs that produced the relationship."
do_2 = "Add the matching mode to the MCP recall input so the verb inventory stays frozen at fourteen: the mode embeds the query in the relation space through the existing embedding runtime, calls the daemon, and renders items whose provenance is the asserting edge LSN and whose support_lsns are the citation LSNs — the manifest-level distinction between a source that produced a relationship and text that merely appeared in context, at the recall surface. Tripwires are guarded over every returned LSN exactly as the vector lane arm already does."
do_3 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::recall(RecallRequest::Relation { .. }) returns RelationResult values ordered by lane rank, each carrying edge_id, relation, source_id, target_id, event_lsn, weight_micros, support_lsns and score_q32. envelope.health['encoder'] is populated for relation mode exactly as it is for semantic mode."

[task.6.6]
title = "Summary hits resolve back to their original evidence as paired activation items"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["6.4"]
reqs = ["6.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/fusion.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/trim.rs", "crates/hm-compose/tests/summaries.rs", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test summaries"
do_1 = "A minted memory is HyperMind's summary: it finds the topic, but its definition is derived text, not the evidence. Today populate_memories (crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs:596) emits the summary alone and lists its citation LSNs as provenance, so the precise original wording never reaches the bundle. Pair every surviving summary with the original observation it cites: immediately after adding a memory item, resolve its first citation LSN to the conversation record it points at, decode it through the existing safety path, and add a second item in the same tier carrying that original content with WhyCode::Evidence and provenance set to the cited LSN alone."
do_2 = "This is pairing, not rank fusion: the evidence item exists only because its summary was selected, inherits the summary's position, and is dropped whenever the summary is dropped. Skip the pairing when the cited record is in the active conversation, is not a semantic kind, is already present in the bundle at that LSN, or fails the safety predicate — the same rules the lexical lane already applies. Bound the work: at most one paired evidence item per summary and at most MAXIMUM_PAIRED_EVIDENCE (64) per bundle, with a TruncatedLane gap when the cap bites."
do_3 = "Prove it: For a bundle containing a memory whose citation points at an observation in another conversation, the Fused section contains the summary item followed immediately by an evidence item whose content is the original observation bytes, whose why is WhyCode::Evidence, and whose provenance is exactly that one cited LSN. The existing bundle, required and safety suites stay green: cargo test -p hm-compose --test bundle, --test required and --test safety all pass."

[task.6.7]
title = "Retrieval manifest records assertion support separately from included text"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["6.6"]
reqs = ["6.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/canonical.rs", "sdk/python/hypermind/bundle.py", "sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/canonical.ts", "sdk/go/bundle.go", "crates/hm-compose/tests/manifest.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/sdk-api.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test manifest"
do_1 = "The retrieval manifest today records candidates, selected, included and used (crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs:183). None of those says whether a source produced a derived claim or merely happened to be quoted into the context. Add a fifth list, support: the ledger LSNs that a surviving derived item cites as the evidence that produced it."
do_2 = "Fill it in activate_with_context after trim, from the citations of surviving summary items and their paired evidence items only — never from lexical or conversation items. Serialize it as the last field of the HMA1 stream, after the four health bytes, and teach the three checked-in SDK decoders to read it before their trailing-bytes check. Leave the manifest_id preimage untouched so stored manifests keep validating under manifest::validate_reuse."
do_3 = "The result is a manifest a caller can audit: included answers what text reached the model, support answers what evidence produced the derived claims in it."
do_4 = "Prove it: RetrievalManifest has pub support: Vec<LSN>, initialized empty in empty_bundle (crates/hm-compose/src/bundle.rs:376-387) and filled after trim in activate_with_context. sdk/python/hypermind/bundle.py, sdk/typescript/packages/client/src/canonical.ts and sdk/go/bundle.go each read one additional LSN array before their trailing-bytes check and still reject a bundle with real trailing bytes."

[task.6.8]
title = "Integer-only geometric alignment math in hm-index"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "index"
requires = []
reqs = ["6.5"]
touches = ["crates/hm-index/src/geometry.rs", "crates/hm-index/src/lib.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-index --lib geometry"
do_1 = "Add the deterministic arithmetic the experimental relevance boost needs, in the crate that already owns integer-only scoring. Provide a Q16 fixed-point cosine over int8 vectors, a projection of a vector onto an ordered set of basis directions yielding one coordinate per direction, an alignment score that is a query-relevance-weighted average of a candidate's per-direction coordinates using the query's positive coordinates as weights, and a multiplicative factor derived from that score. Everything is integer arithmetic with u128/i128 intermediates and u64::isqrt; there are no floats, so scores are bit-reproducible across x86-64 and aarch64, which the determinism suite requires."
do_2 = "The functions are neutral by construction: an empty basis, an empty coordinate vector, a zero-norm vector or a query that aligns with no direction all yield the neutral alignment score and a factor of exactly Q16_ONE, so a caller that supplies nothing leaves ranking untouched. Follow crates/hm-index/src/bm25.rs for module shape, the narrowest cast allows, and inline unit tests."
do_3 = "Prove it: cosine_q16 returns Q16_ONE for identical vectors, 0 for orthogonal vectors, -Q16_ONE for opposed vectors, 0 when either norm is zero, None for a length mismatch and None for an empty pair, and is scale invariant. The module contains no floating-point type and no unsafe code; crates/hm-index/src/lib.rs keeps #![forbid(unsafe_code)]."

[task.6.9]
title = "Version-gated, off-by-default geometric relevance boost in hm-compose"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["6.8"]
reqs = ["6.5"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/geometry.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-compose/tests/geometry.rs", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test geometry"
do_1 = "Expose the geometric alignment math as an experimental rerank option that cannot be switched on without measured evidence. The boost takes the fused hits, the query vector and a map from canonical id to the candidate's stored int8 vector, derives an ordered basis from the first eight hits that have a vector, projects every candidate and the query onto that basis, and multiplies each hit's composite score by the alignment factor. It is off by default: a default GeometryConfig produces an identity transform that touches no score and no order."
do_2 = "Enabling requires an explicit deployment id, a declared version matching GEOMETRY_VERSION, and evidence produced by hm-eval whose measured boosted MRR@10 exceeds its baseline — otherwise opening the boost fails with GeometryError::UnqualifiedDeployment. This is the same gate shape the cross-encoder reranker already uses (crates/hm-compose/src/rerank.rs:68-88), reused deliberately so there is one way to qualify an optional ranking change. Candidates with no stored vector are treated as neutral rather than dropped, and every applied hit's provenance URI records the factor that moved it."
do_3 = "Prove it: AlignmentBoost::open(&GeometryConfig::default()) succeeds, enabled() is false, and apply() leaves both scores and order byte-identical. Nothing in the crate enables the boost: grep shows no construction of GeometryConfig with enabled: true outside tests and hm-eval."

[task.6.10]
title = "hm-eval ablation that measures the geometric boost before it may be enabled"
status = "done"
wave = 6
owner_lane = "eval"
requires = ["6.9"]
reqs = ["6.5"]
touches = ["crates/hm-eval/src/suites/geometry.rs", "crates/hm-eval/src/suites/mod.rs", "crates/hm-eval/src/slice4.rs", "eval/fixtures/geometry/alignment.json", "crates/hm-eval/tests/geometry.rs", "docs/evaluation/methodology.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-eval --test geometry"
do_1 = "No ranking threshold merges without a number, and the geometric boost is gated on evidence produced by hm-eval specifically. Add a network-free evaluation suite that measures the boost as an ablation: build a deterministic corpus from a committed fixture, embed it with the hash-feature embedder, rank each query twice — once by plain int8 dot product and once with hm_compose::geometry::AlignmentBoost applied to the fused hits — and report baseline and boosted MRR@10 side by side together with the fixture digest and the number of queries. The suite never enables the boost anywhere but inside its own measurement, and it reports the default-off state as a metric so a reader can see the lane is disabled."
do_2 = "Wire the three metrics into the slice 4 gate's judge-free list and declare the suite in that gate's suite inventory, with no absolute threshold: this is an experimental lane whose number is published, not a merge blocker. Follow crates/hm-eval/src/suites/attention.rs for suite shape, fixture loading with include_bytes! and the blake3 fixture_hash convention."
do_3 = "Prove it: crates/hm-eval/src/suites/geometry.rs exists, is registered in crates/hm-eval/src/suites/mod.rs alphabetically, and makes no network call, no provider call and no filesystem read outside include_bytes!. No threshold check is added for the geometry metrics: a lower boosted MRR reports a number, it does not fail the gate."

[task.7.1]
title = "Declare the consumed source LSN window on every consolidation run"
status = "done"
wave = 7
section = "Wave 7 - Extraction windows, imported playbooks and improvement proposals"
owner_lane = "l1"
requires = []
reqs = ["7.1"]
touches = ["schemas/events.fbs", "crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs", "crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/import.rs", "crates/hm-eval/src/suites/generations.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/generations.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/sleep.rs", "crates/hm-schema/tests/validation.rs", "docs/reference/generated/schema-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-schema --test validation"
do_1 = "Give a background consolidation run a first-class, persisted statement of which ledger LSNs it consumed, so extraction can be incremental against source positions instead of a mutable count of rows. Append two scalar fields, source_first_lsn and source_last_lsn, to table ConsolidationOpened in schemas/events.fbs and regenerate crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs with planus 1.3.0. Extend validate_consolidation_opened so the pair is either both zero, meaning the run declared no window, or both non-zero with source_first_lsn <= source_last_lsn; anything else is ErrorCode::SchemaInvalid."
do_2 = "Both-zero must stay legal because already-durable frames decode the new fields as zero and crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs re-verifies the whole log at Boundary::Disk on every boot. Update every existing ConsolidationOpened struct literal in the workspace to pass 0 for both fields; this task changes no behaviour beyond making the window expressible. Regenerate the docs catalogs, because docs/reference/generated/schema-types.md embeds the full table declaration."
do_3 = "Prove it: schemas/events.fbs table ConsolidationOpened ends with source_first_lsn:ulong; and source_last_lsn:ulong; and the union EventPayload member order is unchanged. hm_schema::event::verify_event rejects source_first_lsn 9 with source_last_lsn 5, source_first_lsn 0 with source_last_lsn 9, and source_first_lsn 5 with source_last_lsn 0, each with ErrorCode::SchemaInvalid."

[task.7.2]
title = "Extract only above the per-scope watermark and expose it"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["7.1"]
reqs = ["7.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/watermarks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test watermarks"
do_1 = "Make consolidation incremental against source LSN positions. In crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs, carry source_first_lsn and source_last_lsn on RunSummary, populate them in read_history from each ConsolidationOpened payload, and derive a watermark map keyed by scope_digest: the maximum source_last_lsn over runs whose status is RunStatus::Published. Runs whose status became Retracted are excluded, so retracting a run automatically rewinds its scope's watermark and the next run re-reads that window."
do_2 = "In start(), read the watermark for the requested scope and the ledger head from ActorEngine::stats(); declare source_first_lsn = watermark + 1 and source_last_lsn = head; when head <= watermark, append nothing and return an envelope reporting that there is no source material above the watermark. Bound the NREM scan to the declared window with a new nrem_clusters_in_window(actor, first_lsn, last_lsn) that returns the clusters and the count of message frames inside the window, keeping the existing pub nrem_clusters(actor) as a delegating wrapper so crates/hm-sim/tests/slice6_journey.rs still compiles. Surface the window on the run envelope and the watermarks on the list envelope."
do_3 = "Prove it: A first consolidate run over a fresh actor reports source_first_lsn 1 and source_last_lsn equal to the ledger head at open time. crates/hm-mcp/tests/sleep.rs still passes unchanged."

[task.7.3]
title = "Ledger records for imported playbooks and improvement proposals"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l1"
requires = ["7.1"]
reqs = ["7.2", "7.4"]
touches = ["schemas/events.fbs", "crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs", "crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/src/frame.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/checkpoint.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/authority.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/ingest.rs", "crates/hm-schema/tests/anticipation.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/tests/frame.rs", "docs/reference/generated/schema-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-schema -p hm-ledger"
do_1 = "Add the two ledger record types the rest of the group needs. In schemas/events.fbs add table ProcedureImported (procedure_id, name, strategy, expected_outcomes, preconditions, instructions, declared_tools, source_uri, source_digest, playbook_version) and table ProcedureImprovementProposed (proposal_id, procedure_id, base_lsn, strategy, expected_outcomes, preconditions, rationale, failure_lsns), then append both names to union EventPayload in that order. Regenerate crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs with planus 1.3.0."
do_2 = "In crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs add ProcedureImported = 44 and ProcedureImprovementProposed = 45 to EventKind and its TryFrom<u8>, add both to is_wave_seven, add both payload_kind arms, add both validate_payload arms with bounded validators, add MAXIMUM_PLAYBOOK_BYTES, and extend validate_envelope so an imported playbook must carry Authority::ExternalObserved and a proposal must carry Authority::DerivedInference, otherwise ErrorCode::ProtectedTypeWrite. A proposal's failure_lsns are real evidence: validate them through validate::authority::validate_observed_evidence so every cited LSN must be an existing ledger event with observed authority. Mirror the two discriminants in crates/hm-ledger/src/frame.rs (enum plus the KINDS array and its length), map them in crates/hm-proj/src/checkpoint.rs schema_kind, and add the arms the exhaustive matches in crates/hm-cortex/src/authority.rs and crates/hm-cortex/src/ingest.rs demand."
do_3 = "Prove it: EventKind::try_from(44) and (45) yield ProcedureImported and ProcedureImprovementProposed in both hm_schema::event and hm_ledger::frame, with the same numbers, and try_from(46) is an error in both. The existing union member order and every existing event kind number are unchanged."

[task.7.4]
title = "Deterministic playbook document parser in hm-cortex"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = ["7.3"]
reqs = ["7.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/playbook.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/playbooks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test playbooks"
do_1 = "Turn an externally authored playbook document into a ProcedureImported payload with no model call and no I/O. Add crates/hm-cortex/src/playbook.rs, registered in crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs, with parse(source_uri, document) -> Result<ProcedureImported, Error> and procedure_id(source_uri, name) -> Vec<u8>. The document format is the group's HyperMind playbook v1: a first line containing exactly %%, then key: value header lines, then a second line containing exactly %%, then the instruction body. Required keys are name, strategy and outcomes; optional keys are preconditions, tools and version; list values are semicolon-separated. Unknown keys, duplicate keys, missing required keys, empty entries after trimming, an empty body, non-UTF-8 bytes and a document larger than MAXIMUM_DOCUMENT_BYTES all fail closed with a named ErrorCode."
do_2 = "The identifiers are content-derived so that re-importing the same document at the same URI is a detectable duplicate rather than a second procedure. The parser must produce a payload that the real schema admission path accepts, which the test proves by encoding it and calling verify_event with Authority::ExternalObserved."
do_3 = "Prove it: parse returns a ProcedureImported whose name, strategy, expected_outcomes, preconditions, declared_tools and playbook_version come from the header and whose instructions are exactly the bytes after the closing %% line. The parsed payload, encoded into an EventEnvelope with Authority::ExternalObserved, passes hm_schema::event::verify_event at Boundary::Socket for EventKind::ProcedureImported."

[task.7.5]
title = "Store imported playbooks metadata-first in the procedures projection"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l2"
requires = ["7.3", "7.4"]
reqs = ["7.2", "7.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/procedures.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/procedures.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/playbooks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --test playbooks"
do_1 = "Project ProcedureImported into the existing ProjectionId::Procedures database so an imported playbook is a visible but untrusted rung of the learning ladder. Add ProcedureState::Imported as a fourth variant appended after Adopted, and apply an import as three keys in one write transaction: the head ProcedureRecord under P + procedure_id with state Imported and an empty supports list, playbook metadata under I + procedure_id, and the raw instruction bytes under B + procedure_id. Splitting metadata from the body is what makes discovery metadata-first: ProceduresProjection::list scans only the P prefix and ProcedureRecord has no instructions field, so no listing path can return a body; the body is reachable only through playbook_instructions."
do_2 = "A duplicate import of an existing procedure id is ErrorCode::AlreadyExists. Relax the ProcedureAdopted arm so a head in state Imported is adoptable exactly like a head in state Supported, which is safe because the schema already forces Authority::UserAsserted on every ProcedureAdopted envelope. Finally, keep hm-compose compiling and safe: render gains an Imported label and read filters Imported records out entirely, so an unadopted external playbook can never reach an activation bundle."
do_3 = "Prove it: After applying a ProcedureImported frame, ProceduresProjection::get returns a record with state ProcedureState::Imported, empty supports, version_lsn equal to the frame LSN and adopted_lsn zero. hm_compose::procedures::read returns no ActivationItem for a record in state Imported, and hm_compose::procedures::render labels it as an unadopted proposal rather than an instruction."

[task.7.6]
title = "Assemble improvement proposals from failed outcomes in hm-cortex"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l4"
requires = ["7.3", "7.5"]
reqs = ["7.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/procedures.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/proposals.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cortex --test proposals"
do_1 = "Give the kernel a deterministic, model-free way to turn a drafted revision plus failure evidence into an admissible ProcedureImprovementProposed payload. Extend crates/hm-cortex/src/procedures.rs, beside the existing mine, supported and can_adopt, with ProcedureHead, ImprovementDraft and propose_improvement."
do_2 = "The caller supplies the head it drafted against and the replacement strategy, expected outcomes, preconditions and rationale; the function enforces the linkage rules that make the proposal reviewable: the base version must be a real non-zero head version, the failure evidence must be non-empty, strictly increasing and free of zero LSNs, and the draft must differ from the head in at least one of strategy, expected outcomes or preconditions so a no-op proposal cannot be recorded. The function never mutates anything and never calls a provider; the observed-evidence check on the failure LSNs is the schema layer's job at admission."
do_3 = "Prove it: propose_improvement returns a ProcedureImprovementProposed whose procedure_id and base_lsn come from the head and whose strategy, expected outcomes, preconditions, rationale and failure_lsns come from the caller unchanged. The function performs no I/O and makes no LlmProvider call."

[task.7.7]
title = "Project improvement proposals with stale-version checks and immutable versions"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l2"
requires = ["7.5"]
reqs = ["7.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/procedures.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/proposals.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --test proposals"
do_1 = "Record improvement proposals in ProjectionId::Procedures without ever overwriting an adopted procedure. Applying a ProcedureImprovementProposed frame writes one record under R + procedure_id + proposed_lsn big-endian and leaves the head under P + procedure_id byte-identical; the target head must exist (ErrorCode::OrderingViolation) and its version_lsn must equal the proposal's base_lsn (ErrorCode::IdempotencyConflict), which is the stale-version check. Extend the ProcedureAdopted arm with a second, additive path: when procedure_lsn does not match the head version but does name a stored proposal whose base_lsn still equals the head version and whose adopted_lsn is zero, snapshot the outgoing head under V + procedure_id + version_lsn big-endian, install a new head carrying the proposal's strategy, expected outcomes and preconditions with state Adopted, previous_lsn set to the outgoing version and version_lsn/adopted_lsn set to the adoption LSN, and stamp adopted_lsn on the proposal record."
do_2 = "The existing head-adoption path and its error codes are unchanged. Add readers for one proposal, a procedure's proposals, and a superseded version."
do_3 = "Prove it: Applying a proposal frame leaves ProceduresProjection::get byte-identical to before and makes ProceduresProjection::proposal return the stored proposal with adopted_lsn zero. canonical_dump(ProjectionId::Procedures) is byte-identical between a full rebuild and a split rebuild of the same frame stream."

[task.7.8]
title = "Admit playbooks and proposals in the actor and expose their reads"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["7.7"]
reqs = ["7.2", "7.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/playbooks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --test playbooks"
do_1 = "Enforce the playbook and proposal preconditions before the ledger commit, and give surfaces a way to read them. In crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs extend WriterState::validate_anticipation with three arms: a ProcedureImported whose procedure_id already exists is ErrorCode::AlreadyExists; a ProcedureImprovementProposed must target an existing head whose version_lsn equals its base_lsn, otherwise OrderingViolation or IdempotencyConflict; and ProcedureAdopted now succeeds either against a head in state Supported or Imported at the named version, or against a stored proposal at the named LSN whose base_lsn still matches the head and whose adopted_lsn is zero, otherwise OrderingViolation. Extend the in-batch anticipation identity table so two imports of one procedure or two proposals with one proposal_id in the same batch are an IdempotencyConflict."
do_2 = "Add three ActorEngine commands and methods that read the new projection records through a snapshot on the writer thread, mirroring the existing Command::Procedure handler. Prove the whole path survives a restart, because boot re-verifies and re-projects the entire log."
do_3 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::append of a valid ProcedureImported succeeds and ActorEngine::procedure reports state Imported; a second import with the same procedure_id is rejected with ErrorCode::AlreadyExists and nothing is appended. After ActorEngine::shutdown and reopening the same directory, every read above returns the same values, proving the log replays at Boundary::Disk."

[task.7.9]
title = "Import, discover and review playbooks through the frozen verb inventory"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["7.4", "7.6", "7.8"]
reqs = ["7.3", "7.5"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/intend.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/playbooks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test playbooks"
do_1 = "Close the vertical: let an agent import a playbook, discover procedures by metadata alone, pull one body on demand, and propose and adopt an improvement, all without a new MCP verb. Add two IntendAction variants: ImportPlaybook parses the document through hm_cortex::playbook::parse and appends the ProcedureImported event with Authority::ExternalObserved, and ProposeProcedureImprovement reads the current head through ActorEngine::procedure, builds the payload through hm_cortex::procedures::propose_improvement and appends it with Authority::DerivedInference. This requires threading an explicit authority through the shared append tuple in intend::run, which today hard-codes UserAsserted."
do_2 = "Add two hm:// URIs to inspect::run, placed before the fall-through to parse_lsn: hm://<actor>/procedures lists procedure metadata and playbook metadata and never returns an instruction body, and hm://<actor>/procedures/<hex procedure_id> returns that procedure with its instructions and its improvement proposals. Adoption of both an imported head and a proposal goes through the existing AdoptProcedure action unchanged."
do_3 = "Prove it: intend with action import_playbook appends one ProcedureImported event and returns its procedure_id and LSN in the envelope. intend with action adopt_procedure naming the proposal LSN advances the head and stamps adopted_lsn on the proposal."

[task.7.10]
title = "Prove unadopted playbooks never reach an activation bundle"
status = "done"
wave = 7
owner_lane = "l5"
requires = ["7.5"]
reqs = ["7.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/tests/playbooks.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --test playbooks"
do_1 = "Lock down the untrusted-until-adopted guarantee at the surface that matters most: the prompt. Add a hm-compose integration test that builds a real frame stream containing an imported playbook and a mined, supported and adopted procedure, rebuilds the projections into a temporary store, and calls hm_compose::procedures::read for a why/how query. An unadopted imported playbook must produce no ActivationItem at all, so its external text can never enter a rendered prompt."
do_2 = "After a ProcedureAdopted frame the same procedure must produce exactly one Fused-tier item with Authority::DerivedInference whose content carries the adopted-instruction label and the ladder metadata, and which still does not carry the playbook instruction body, because the body is disclosed only through the inspect surface. The test also pins the render label for the Imported state so a future change to that string is a deliberate act."
do_3 = "Prove it: With an imported but unadopted playbook in the projection, hm_compose::procedures::read returns no item for it while still returning the item for a separately adopted mined procedure. The test uses a real ProjectionStore rebuilt from real frames and a deterministic TokenCounter."

[task.8.1]
title = "Bounded actor-local ranking preference derived from attestation events"
status = "done"
wave = 8
section = "Wave 8 - Ranking preference learned from attestations"
owner_lane = "projections"
requires = []
reqs = ["8.1", "8.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/attestations.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/preferences.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-proj --locked --test preferences"
do_1 = "Extend the attestations projection so that every Attestation event, besides bumping its disposition counter, also advances a bounded ranking preference for its target LSN. Add a second key prefix P (0x50) inside ProjectionId::Attestations holding a PreferenceWeight record; the existing T-prefixed AttestationRecord and its bincode layout stay byte-identical so no on-disk migration is needed. The weight starts at PREFERENCE_NEUTRAL_Q16 and moves toward a per-disposition target by an integer streaming step, clamped into [PREFERENCE_MINIMUM_Q16, PREFERENCE_MAXIMUM_Q16]; helpful and used raise it, ignored and harmful lower it, and no sequence of events can leave the band. Both mutations go into the one store.apply batch that already carries the checkpoint, so the weight is atomic with the counter and replay-idempotent."
do_2 = "Add read APIs for one target, for a bounded set of targets, and for the most recent weights. The projection remains the only writer; nothing about beliefs, memories, graph edges or authority is touched. Consumers are g08-t2 (fusion) and g08-t4 (the inspect surface)."
do_3 = "Prove it: Applying an Attestation event with disposition helpful to target LSN 3 leaves AttestationsProjection::preference(snapshot, LSN::new(3)) with weight_q16 strictly greater than PREFERENCE_NEUTRAL_Q16 and at most PREFERENCE_MAXIMUM_Q16. AttestationsProjection::preferences(snapshot, targets) returns ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded when targets exceeds MAXIMUM_PREFERENCE_TARGETS and ErrorCode::InvalidArgument for a zero LSN."

[task.8.2]
title = "Preference profile and preference-aware reciprocal rank fusion"
status = "done"
wave = 8
owner_lane = "compose"
requires = ["8.1"]
reqs = ["8.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-compose/src/preference.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-compose/src/fusion.rs", "crates/hm-compose/tests/preference.rs", "docs/concepts/retrieval.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-compose --locked --test preference"
do_1 = "Add a read-side preference module to hm-compose that loads the bounded weights written by g08-t1 for a specific, bounded set of evidence LSNs and exposes the single score-adjust function the whole system shares. Add a preference-aware fusion entry point beside the existing one: the composite still multiplies reciprocal rank fusion by fsrs retrievability, salience factor and recency prior exactly as today, and the bounded preference is applied to that composite afterwards, so a maximally preferred item can gain at most a quarter and a maximally disfavoured item can lose at most a quarter. The existing fuse function keeps its exact signature and behaviour by delegating with a neutral profile, so every current test, URI string and acceptance criterion is unchanged."
do_2 = "FusedHit gains a preference_q16 field and the provenance URI gains a &pref= parameter, appended only when the weight is not neutral. The profile is loaded from one ReadSnapshot and never reads anything outside the actor's own projection environment. The consumer is g08-t3, which uses PreferenceProfile and adjust_q32 on the daemon recall path."
do_3 = "Prove it: fuse(actor, conversation, rankings, limit) and fuse_with_preferences(actor, conversation, rankings, limit, &PreferenceProfile::neutral()) return equal Vec<FusedHit> values for the same input, and every hit has preference_q16 == Q16_ONE and a URI containing no pref=. Item content, authority and provenance LSNs are never read or altered by the preference module; it only maps LSN to weight."

[task.8.3]
title = "Recall applies the actor's bounded ranking preferences"
status = "done"
wave = 8
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["8.1", "8.2"]
reqs = ["8.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/preferences.rs", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --locked --test preferences"
do_1 = "Make the daemon's recall path consume the actor's own ranking preferences so feedback on one answer visibly changes the next answer's evidence order. Inside ActorEngine's recall, after the lane dispatch produces its RecallItem list, load a PreferenceProfile for exactly the returned LSNs from the same read snapshot, adjust each item's score_q32 through hm_compose::preference::adjust_q32, record the weight on the item, and re-sort by score descending then LSN ascending. Only the score-bearing modes participate (vector, lexical, entity, near); temporal and timeline keep their chronological order untouched."
do_2 = "When the profile is neutral the function returns the list exactly as the lane produced it, so behaviour with no feedback is bit-for-bit what it is today. Surface the weight in the MCP recall envelope as a preference_q16 field and as an appended &pref= parameter on the item URI, only when the weight is not neutral. No wire schema changes: the UDS recall response still carries LSNs, so the reordering propagates through every surface for free."
do_3 = "Prove it: With no attestation events in the ledger, an MCP lexical recall over a remembered document returns exactly the same items, in the same order, with the same score_q32 values and the same URIs as before this change, and every item reports preference_q16 == 65536 with no pref= in its URI. After actor.shutdown() and reopening the same actor directory, the same recall returns the same adjusted scores and order, proving the preference is rebuilt from the ledger and not held in memory."

[task.8.4]
title = "Preference inspection surface inside the inspect verb and actor isolation proof"
status = "done"
wave = 8
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["8.1", "8.3"]
reqs = ["8.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/preference_surface.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --locked --test preference_surface"
do_1 = "Make the learned ranking preferences readable and auditable without adding an MCP verb. Add a bounded read command to ActorEngine that returns the most recent preference weights from the attestations projection, and resolve hm://<actor>/preferences inside the existing inspect verb exactly the way hm://<actor>/attention and hm://<actor>/calibration are already resolved: an items[0].preferences array with the target LSN, the Q16 weight, the observation count and the last attestation LSN, plus one provenance entry per target. A preferences URI naming any other actor is not this surface and falls through to the existing LSN parser, which rejects it, so one actor can never read another actor's ranking preferences through this verb."
do_2 = "Prove isolation end to end with two real actors in separate directories: feedback in one leaves the other's preference list empty and its recall scores neutral. Update the inspect guidance in docs/tools/usage.json and the MCP reference prose so the docs gate stays green."
do_3 = "Prove it: inspect with uri hm://7/preferences on an actor with three attested targets returns ok, and items[0]['preferences'] is an array of three objects each carrying target_lsn, weight_q16, observations and last_attestation_lsn, ordered by target_lsn descending. The existing hm://7/attention and hm://7/calibration surfaces and the provenance-chain behaviour of inspect are unchanged."

[task.9.1]
title = "Provider call admission independent of spend budgets"
status = "done"
wave = 9
section = "Wave 9 - Admission, bounded extraction and daemon leases"
owner_lane = "l3"
requires = []
reqs = ["9.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-llm/src/admission.rs", "crates/hm-llm/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-llm/tests/admission.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-llm --locked"
do_1 = "Give hm-llm a bound on how many provider calls may be in flight at once, separate from the money and token budgets that already exist in hm_llm::cost. Add crates/hm-llm/src/admission.rs holding AdmissionLimits (a global in-flight ceiling, a per-actor share and a bounded wait in milliseconds), CallAdmission (the shared gate), AdmissionPermit (an RAII hold released on drop) and AdmittedProvider<P> (an LlmProvider wrapper that takes a permit for the duration of one structured call and releases it as soon as the response has been decoded). The gate is blocking and uses only std::sync::Mutex plus std::sync::Condvar, matching the rest of hm-llm, which has no async runtime and no tokio dependency."
do_2 = "A caller that cannot be admitted inside its wait is refused with a new LlmError::Admission variant carrying a static reason, so an admission refusal can never be mistaken for the spend refusal LlmError::Capacity. Fairness is the per-actor cap: no actor may occupy more than its configured share of the global ceiling, so one busy actor cannot starve the others. A ceiling of zero is clamped to one so a misconfigured deployment serialises instead of deadlocking, and a wait of zero means 'only if a slot is free right now'. Also add a blanket impl of LlmProvider for Arc<P> so an already-boxed Arc<dyn LlmProvider> can be wrapped without unwrapping it."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_llm::admission::CallAdmission::new(AdmissionLimits { maximum_in_flight: 2, maximum_in_flight_per_actor: 1, maximum_wait_ms: 0 }) admits actor 7, refuses a second concurrent admit for actor 7 with LlmError::Admission, admits actor 8, and refuses actor 9 with LlmError::Admission; dropping the actor 7 permit then lets actor 9 in. AdmittedProvider wrapping a real OpenAiCompatible<RecordedTransport> returns the recorded StructuredResponse unchanged, leaves in_flight() at 0 afterwards, reports high_water_mark() == 1, and leaves transport().remaining() == 0."

[task.9.2]
