do_1 = "Put the admission gate from g09-t1 on the two production provider paths in hm-mcp so the bound is real rather than library-only. Add crates/hm-mcp/src/admission.rs with a single env reader that builds a shared CallAdmission for the process from HM_PROVIDER_MAX_IN_FLIGHT, HM_PROVIDER_MAX_IN_FLIGHT_PER_ACTOR and HM_PROVIDER_ADMISSION_WAIT_MS, falling back to AdmissionLimits::default() when a variable is absent or unparsable. Give ReconstructionRuntime and ConsolidationRuntime an admission field and a provider_for(actor) accessor that returns the configured provider wrapped in AdmittedProvider for that actor id, and change both call sites to use it: crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs takes the provider for actor.actor().get() before spawn_blocking, and the NREM branch of crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs does the same before consolidate_clusters."
do_2 = "Add the LlmError::Admission arm to the error map in reconstruct.rs so a refusal surfaces as ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded rather than falling through. Add ReconstructionRuntime::new so the two existing struct literals in crates/hm-mcp/tests/reconstruction_surface.rs keep compiling with the new field. Admission bounds concurrent calls only; the consolidation budget fields max_llm_calls, max_tokens, max_microusd and max_wall_ms are untouched and still enforced exactly as before."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_mcp::admission::admission_from_env() returns an Arc<CallAdmission> whose limits equal AdmissionLimits::default() when none of the three environment variables is set, and equal the parsed values when all three are set to valid integers. docs/reference/config.md documents the three environment variables, their defaults, and states explicitly that they bound concurrent calls and are not a spend limit."

[task.9.3]
title = "Per-cluster extraction entry point with one recorded outcome per candidate"
status = "done"
