do_1 = "Split the NREM merge loop in crates/hm-cortex/src/nrem/merge.rs into a per-candidate entry point so a scheduler can drive one cluster at a time and record exactly one outcome for it. Add extract_cluster, which builds the merge request, makes at most one structured provider call, validates the response and returns a ClusterExtraction carrying either a decision or a typed drop, the provider Usage, how many provider calls were actually made, and whether the drop was a citation failure."
do_2 = "A cluster whose merge request cannot be built is returned as a drop with zero calls and zero usage, so the caller can tell a candidate that was never paid for from one that was. Rewrite consolidate_clusters as a fold over extract_cluster that produces exactly the NremReport it produces today - same decisions, same dropped candidates in the same order, same citation_invalid count, same llm_calls, same RunCost - so the existing hm-cortex vectors keep passing unchanged. hm-cortex stays synchronous and tokio-free; nothing about concurrency enters this crate."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_cortex::nrem::merge::extract_cluster returns Ok(ClusterExtraction) for a cluster whose provider call succeeds and whose response validates, with outcome ClusterOutcome::Decided, llm_calls == 1 and usage equal to the provider's reported Usage. consolidate_clusters keeps its exact signature and behaviour: the existing test in crates/hm-cortex/tests/nrem.rs that drives three clusters through a RecordedTransport and asserts llm_calls == 3, decisions.len() == 1, citation_invalid == 1 and both drop reasons passes unchanged."

[task.9.4]
title = "Bounded-concurrency extraction scheduler with per-item outcomes and restored source order"
status = "done"
wave = 9
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["9.2"]
reqs = ["9.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/extraction.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/Cargo.toml", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/extraction.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --locked --test extraction"
do_1 = "Add crates/hm-mcp/src/extraction.rs, the scheduler that runs background extraction work over a list of candidates with a hard ceiling on how many run at once, records one outcome per item, and hands the caller back the results in source order. Each item is dispatched to tokio::task::spawn_blocking behind a tokio::sync::Semaphore whose permit is held for the whole blocking call, so the ceiling is on work actually running, not on work queued. A permit is taken before the item is admitted, and the stop flag is read at that exact moment - the last point at which a paid call can still be avoided."
do_2 = "When stop_dispatch_on_failure is set and an item has already failed, the remaining items are recorded as skipped and never dispatched, while everything already admitted runs to completion and is collected; nothing in flight is cancelled and nothing already paid for is discarded. Outcomes are carried out of the concurrent region with their zero-based source index and sorted back into source order before returning, so extracted, failed, skipped and aborted are each ascending by index. A maximum_parallel of zero is clamped to one."
do_3 = "The module is generic over the item, the value and the error so it carries no cognition knowledge; g09-t5 is its consumer."
do_4 = "Prove it: hm_mcp::extraction::extract_bounded over 32 items with maximum_parallel 4 never has more than 4 work closures running at once, observed through an AtomicUsize peak owned by the test closure. An empty item list returns an ExtractionOutcomes whose four vectors are all empty without spawning anything."

[task.9.5]
title = "Run NREM consolidation through bounded extraction and report per-candidate outcomes"
status = "done"
