do_1 = "Make the NREM phase of a consolidation run use the bounded scheduler from g09-t4 over the per-cluster entry point from g09-t3, so a run with many candidates makes several provider calls at once under a ceiling instead of one strictly at a time, and so every candidate ends with a recorded outcome. Give ConsolidationRuntime a maximum_parallel setting with a with_parallelism builder and an HM_CONSOLIDATION_PARALLEL environment override clamped to 1..=64, defaulting to 4. Replace the consolidate_clusters call in the Nrem branch of crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs with extract_bounded over the retained clusters, stop_dispatch_on_failure set, and rebuild the same aggregates the branch already keeps: llm_calls, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_microusd and dropped_candidates, now also folding skipped and aborted candidates into dropped_candidates."
do_2 = "Keep the budget post-check byte-identical: a run that exceeds max_llm_calls, max_tokens or max_microusd still returns ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded. Surface the four per-item counts in the run envelope under items[0].extraction so an operator can see what succeeded, what the provider refused and what was never dispatched, without touching the frozen event schema. The clusters are processed in source order on return, so the staged MemoryMinted events are emitted in exactly the order the clusters were produced."
do_3 = "Prove it: A consolidate run action with a ConsolidationRuntime at parallelism 1 over N mint-eligible clusters, each with a matching recorded fixture, publishes the run, emits one MemoryMinted per minted decision, leaves the recorded transport exhausted, and reports items[0].extraction == { extracted: N, failed: 0, skipped: 0, aborted: 0 }. HM_CONSOLIDATION_PARALLEL of '0', '' or a non-number yields the default of 4 rather than a failure, and a value above 64 is clamped to 64."

[task.9.6]
title = "Actor-aware resource leases with RAII release and pinning"
status = "done"
wave = 9
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = []
reqs = ["9.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/leases.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/leases.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --locked --test leases"
do_1 = "Add crates/hm-serve/src/leases.rs, a registry that bounds how many actors may be simultaneously active inside one daemon and how many heavyweight jobs may run at once, and hands out leases that release themselves on drop. A lease is taken for an actor and a class: LeaseClass::Actor is the ordinary hold a request takes for the life of that request, LeaseClass::HeavyJob additionally consumes one of the heavyweight-job slots that projection rebuilds, key destruction and bulk ingestion share. The registry keeps one semaphore permit and one depth counter per actor: the first lease for an actor takes the permit, every further lease for that same actor increments the depth and returns immediately, and the permit is released only when the last lease is dropped."
do_2 = "That is the pinning rule - an actor whose work is already admitted can never be refused or starved by a newly arriving actor. A lease that cannot be granted waits at most LeaseLimits::wait_ms and is then refused with hm_core::ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded rather than queueing forever; a wait of zero means take a slot only if one is free right now. A limit of zero is clamped to one so a misconfigured daemon serialises rather than deadlocks."
do_3 = "The registry is cheaply cloneable and exposes a snapshot of active actors, active leases, running heavy jobs and cumulative refusals. g09-t7 is its consumer."
do_4 = "Prove it: LeaseRegistry::new(LeaseLimits { maximum_active_actors: 1, maximum_heavy_jobs: 1, wait_ms: 0 }) grants an Actor lease to actor 7, refuses actor 8 with ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded, and grants a second Actor lease to actor 7 immediately because actor 7 is already pinned. LeaseRegistry is Clone and Send + Sync, ActorLease is Send, and no acquire holds a std mutex across an await."

[task.9.7]
title = "Hold resource leases across daemon requests and configure them per deployment"
status = "done"
wave = 9
owner_lane = "l6"
requires = ["9.6"]
reqs = ["9.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/config.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/uds.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/config.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/uds.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/admin.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/remote.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/continuity.rs", "crates/hm-cli/tests/import.rs", "docs/reference/config.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --locked --test config --test uds --test admin"
do_1 = "Make the lease registry from g09-t6 real inside the daemon. Add three keys to the hypermind.conf loader - maximum_active_actors, maximum_heavy_jobs and lease_wait_ms - with the same bounded-parse discipline the existing numeric keys use, and add the matching ServerConfig fields. Build one LeaseRegistry in UdsServer::bind from those limits, expose it with a leases() accessor so an operator surface and the tests can read its snapshot, and thread it through serve_until and handle_connection into handle_request."
do_2 = "In handle_request, once the target actor id has been resolved, take an Actor lease and hold it in a binding that lives until the response payload has been produced, so the lease covers the whole request and is released by Drop on every path including the error paths. RebuildProjection and CryptoDelete take a HeavyJob lease instead, so a rebuild can never run while the daemon's heavyweight-job slots are full. A refusal is returned as ErrorCode::CapacityExceeded, which the existing effect-state table classifies conservatively as unknown; that classification is left untouched."
do_3 = "Update the five hand-built ServerConfig literals in the test suites, document the keys in docs/reference/config.md and regenerate the config-key catalog."
do_4 = "Prove it: hypermind.conf accepts maximum_active_actors (default 64, range 1 to 4096), maximum_heavy_jobs (default 2, range 1 to 256) and lease_wait_ms (default 250, range 0 to 60000); a value outside the range is rejected with ErrorCode::InvalidArgument and an unknown key is still rejected as before. crates/hm-serve/tests/{uds,admin,remote,continuity}.rs and crates/hm-cli/tests/import.rs compile with the three new ServerConfig fields and pass unchanged in behaviour."

[task.10.1]
title = "C ABI crate with explicit handle ownership, status tier and drift-checked header"
status = "done"
wave = 10
section = "Wave 10 - The C ABI and the Apple-platform package"
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = []
reqs = ["10.1"]
touches = ["Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "crates/hm-capi/Cargo.toml", "crates/hm-capi/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-capi/src/status.rs", "crates/hm-capi/src/engine.rs", "crates/hm-capi/include/hypermind.h", "crates/hm-capi/tests/lifecycle.rs", "crates/hm-capi/tests/header.rs", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-capi --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Create the hm-capi crate: the C-callable edge of the embedded kernel. It owns an opaque HmEngine handle over hm_serve::actor::ActorEngine plus a per-handle Tokio runtime and an hm_mcp::dispatcher::McpToolDispatcher, and it publishes the boundary status tier, the thread-local last-error slot and the string-release function that every later entry point depends on. Handle lifecycle is explicit and split three ways: hm_engine_open builds the state, hm_engine_clone shares it by reference count, hm_engine_close deterministically shuts the actor down for every clone, and hm_engine_free releases exactly one pointer."
do_2 = "Configuration arrives as a strict JSON object carrying the actor id and the sealed-identity material, so an embedder never passes raw key bytes positionally. The C header is hand-authored and locked against the Rust source by a test that reconciles three sources: the exported-function names scraped from the crate's own source text, the HM_EXPORTED_SYMBOLS and HM_STATUS_TABLE constants, and the declarations in the header. No MCP verb, schema, protocol, REST route or config key is added or changed by this task."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_abi_version() returns (1 << 16) | 0, and the header defines HM_ABI_VERSION_MAJOR 1 and HM_ABI_VERSION_MINOR 0. crates/hm-capi/tests/header.rs passes and fails loudly on drift: it asserts the set of hm_* function names scraped from crates/hm-capi/src/*.rs equals HM_EXPORTED_SYMBOLS exactly, that the set of hm_* declarations in include/hypermind.h equals HM_EXPORTED_SYMBOLS exactly, that every HM_STATUS_<NAME> = <value> enumerator in the header matches HM_STATUS_TABLE, that HM_STATUS_TABLE matches HmStatus::<Variant> as i32 for all eight variants, and that HM_ABI_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR in the header reproduce hm_abi_version()."

[task.10.2]
title = "Deferred verb-call entry point, kernel error mapping and synchronous waiter"
status = "done"
wave = 10
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["10.1"]
reqs = ["10.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-capi/src/call.rs", "crates/hm-capi/src/waiter.rs", "crates/hm-capi/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-capi/src/engine.rs", "crates/hm-capi/include/hypermind.h", "crates/hm-capi/tests/call.rs", "crates/hm-capi/tests/header.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-capi --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Give the C ABI its one operation entry point. hm_engine_call takes a verb name and an arguments JSON document, clones the handle's ActorEngine, and runs McpToolDispatcher::dispatch on the handle's own Tokio runtime, delivering the serialized tool envelope through a callback that always fires exactly once and always on a worker thread. Kernel failures are translated once and precisely: HM_STATUS_KERNEL plus the numeric hm_core::ErrorCode discriminant plus its stable kInvalidArgument-style name, so a C consumer can branch on the exact kernel code without parsing prose. A dispatch panic is contained through the inner join handle and surfaces as HM_STATUS_PANIC instead of unwinding across the FFI boundary."
do_2 = "For embedders that cannot host a callback, a single-use HmWaiter turns any call into a blocking one, hands the caller an owned result string, and refuses both reuse and a wait issued from a runtime worker thread. The MCP verb inventory is not touched: an unknown verb reaches the existing dispatcher and comes back as kCapabilityDenied."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm_engine_call returns HM_STATUS_OK and the callback is invoked exactly once for a valid remember call; a test counter proves one invocation and the callback's std::thread::current().id() differs from the caller's. HM_ABI_VERSION_MINOR is raised to 1 in both the header and crates/hm-capi/src/lib.rs, and the header-version assertion in tests/header.rs still holds."

[task.10.3]
title = "Real C consumer compiled with cc and linked against the shared library"
status = "done"
wave = 10
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["10.2"]
reqs = ["10.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-capi/tests/c/hm_abi_smoke.c", "crates/hm-capi/tests/c_abi.rs"]
verify_cmd = "cargo build -p hm-capi --locked && cargo test -p hm-capi --locked --test c_abi"
do_1 = "Prove the C ABI from C, not only from Rust. A small C program includes the published header, opens an engine on a directory handed to it on the command line, drives remember and recall through the synchronous waiter, checks the unknown-verb kernel path, releases every string and handle in the documented order, and prints a single success marker. A Rust integration test compiles that program with the system C compiler against crates/hm-capi/include, links it to the built libhypermind.so, runs it with a tempfile::tempdir() argument and asserts a zero exit status with the marker on stdout."
do_2 = "This is the task that turns the header from documentation into a contract: a wrong parameter order, a wrong enumerator value or a missing symbol becomes a compile or link failure rather than a silent mismatch. Nothing in the crate's Rust surface changes, so no catalog regeneration is required."
do_3 = "Prove it: crates/hm-capi/tests/c/hm_abi_smoke.c compiles with cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra against crates/hm-capi/include/hypermind.h with no warnings and links against libhypermind.so with no undefined symbols. The test passes under cargo build -p hm-capi --locked && cargo test -p hm-capi --locked --test c_abi, and the whole crate still passes under cargo test -p hm-capi --locked after a workspace build."

[task.10.4]
title = "Swift async package over the C ABI with a Linux binding-fidelity gate"
status = "done"
wave = 10
owner_lane = "sdk"
requires = ["10.3"]
reqs = ["10.4"]
touches = ["sdk/swift/Package.swift", "sdk/swift/Sources/CHyperMind/module.modulemap", "sdk/swift/Sources/HyperMind/HyperMindCredentials.swift", "sdk/swift/Sources/HyperMind/HyperMindError.swift", "sdk/swift/Sources/HyperMind/ContinuationBox.swift", "sdk/swift/Sources/HyperMind/HyperMindEngine.swift", "sdk/swift/Tests/HyperMindTests/HyperMindEngineTests.swift", "sdk/swift/README.md", "crates/hm-capi/tests/swift_binding.rs", "docs/reference/sdks.md", "sdk/README.md"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-capi --locked --test swift_binding && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Deliver the Apple-platform package honestly. A SwiftPM package under sdk/swift wraps the C header through a system-library target and exposes an async/await surface: a credentials value carrying the actor id and sealed-identity material, an engine class that bridges each hm_engine_call into withCheckedThrowingContinuation by handing a retained continuation box across the void * user-data pointer, a typed error carrying the boundary status, the kernel error code and its stable name, and one thin method per existing HyperMind verb so the fourteen-verb inventory is mirrored rather than widened. Ownership is explicit on both sides: the engine class frees its handle exactly once in deinit, close() is separate and idempotent, result strings are copied inside the callback before it returns, and the continuation box is released exactly once because the callback fires exactly once."
do_2 = "Cancellation is cooperative at the call boundary - checked before the call is issued and after it resolves - because the underlying kernel round trip is not interruptible; that limitation is written down rather than papered over. Swift cannot be compiled in this environment, so the checked-in gate is a Rust test that proves the Swift sources and the module map bind only symbols, status enumerators and verbs that really exist."
do_3 = "Prove it: sdk/swift/Package.swift declares swift-tools-version: 5.9, platforms .macOS(.v13) and .iOS(.v16), a .systemLibrary(name: 'CHyperMind', path: 'Sources/CHyperMind') target, a .target(name: 'HyperMind', dependencies: ['CHyperMind'], path: 'Sources/HyperMind') and a .testTarget(name: 'HyperMindTests', dependencies: ['HyperMind'], path: 'Tests/HyperMindTests'), and a .library(name: 'HyperMind', targets: ['HyperMind']) product. sdk/swift/README.md contains a ## Apple-platform gate section stating that the package is not built or tested by this repository's Linux CI, that no Swift test run is claimed, and giving the two commands a macOS developer needs (cargo rustc -p hm-capi --crate-type staticlib --release and swift test); crates/hm-capi/tests/swift_binding.rs asserts the heading is present so the statement cannot be silently dropped."

[task.11.1]
title = "Signed portable archive: pack the native transfer format with an owned-member allowlist"
status = "done"
wave = 11
section = "Wave 11 - Portable archives, opt-in telemetry and progressive discovery"
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = []
reqs = ["11.1"]
touches = ["crates/hm-ledger/src/checkpoint.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/archive.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/transfer.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cli/tests/archive.rs", "docs/reference/cli.md", "docs/reference/generated/cli-declarations.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cli --test archive --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Introduce hypermind.archive.v1, a single-file portable package around the existing hypermind.events.v1 transfer format, and the hm archive pack and hm archive verify commands that produce and check it. Refactor crates/hm-cli/src/transfer.rs so the JSONL export body is produced once into memory by a new export_stream helper that both hm export and the archive packer call, leaving hm export's observable JSON output unchanged. The packer collects only members named in the owned-member allowlist — the exported event stream and, when a signed MMR checkpoint exists, its 164 encoded bytes — hashes each with blake3, builds the canonical manifest digest, and signs it with the actor's existing Ed25519 checkpoint signing key through two new helpers in crates/hm-ledger/src/checkpoint.rs."
do_2 = "Packing is an offline operation guarded by the existing actors::operation_lock and actors::require_offline, and writes the archive with create_new at mode 0600 followed by sync_all on the file and its parent directory, exactly as transfer::export already does. hm archive verify re-reads an archive with no decryption key at all: it re-derives every member digest, re-derives the manifest digest, verifies the Ed25519 signature against the manifest's own public key, and additionally requires equality with an operator-pinned --public-key when one is supplied. Bounds are enforced on the read path before any base64 decoding so a hostile file cannot force an allocation. This task does not write member files to disk; that is g11-t2."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm archive pack --config PATH --output FILE --json on an actor with events writes FILE with mode 0600 and prints {'ok':true,'format':'hypermind.archive.v1','archive_version':1,'actor':N,'events':N,'members':[...],'public_key':'<64 hex>','bytes':N}. A pack whose total archive size would exceed MAXIMUM_ARCHIVE_BYTES fails with an explicit error rather than writing a partial file."

[task.11.2]
title = "Safe archive unpacking and archive-aware import"
status = "done"
wave = 11
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = ["11.1"]
reqs = ["11.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cli/src/archive.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/transfer.rs", "crates/hm-cli/tests/archive_unpack.rs", "docs/reference/cli.md", "docs/reference/generated/cli-declarations.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-cli --test archive_unpack --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Consume the archive produced by g11-t1: add hm archive unpack --input FILE --output DIR and teach hm import to accept an archive directly. Unpacking runs the full g11-t1 verification first and only then materialises members, so an archive that fails signature, digest, length or bound checks never reaches the filesystem. Member names are validated by exact equality against OWNED_MEMBERS before any path is constructed; a name is additionally rejected if it is duplicated, is empty, contains a path separator, a backslash, a colon, a NUL, .., or any character outside [a-z0-9._-]."
do_2 = "The destination path is built by joining the validated basename onto the caller's directory and then asserted to have that directory as its immediate parent, so a traversal attempt cannot escape even if an earlier check were bypassed. Every written file uses create_new(true).mode(0o600) so unpack never overwrites, followed by sync_all on the file and the directory. transfer::import gains one branch: when the first line's format equals the archive format it verifies the archive, extracts the events.jsonl member and feeds those bytes into the existing native import path unchanged, preserving the hypermind.events.v1 fallback to crate::import::run for anything else. That branch is the vertical consumer: an archive packed from one actor directory imports into a freshly initialised one and the content is recallable."
do_3 = "Prove it: hm archive unpack --input FILE --output DIR --json writes exactly the manifest's members into DIR, each at mode 0600, and prints {'ok':true,'verified':true,'format':'hypermind.archive.v1','actor':N,'members':[{'name':...,'bytes':N,'path':...}]}. hm import with a plain hypermind.events.v1 file and with a cortex-import file behaves exactly as before (no regression in crates/hm-cli/tests/import.rs)."

[task.11.3]
title = "Opt-in metadata-only span export with request spans and shutdown flushing"
status = "done"
wave = 11
owner_lane = "kernel-edge"
requires = []
reqs = ["11.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-core/src/telemetry.rs", "crates/hm-core/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/telemetry.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/uds.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/telemetry.rs", "docs/reference/cli.md", "docs/reference/generated/cli-declarations.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --test telemetry --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Add the HyperMind span model and its opt-in OTLP/JSON file exporter, and instrument the daemon request path with it. crates/hm-core/src/telemetry.rs defines the whole model with no new dependency: SpanKind, SpanOutcome, Attribute, SpanRecord, the SpanSink trait, the process-wide OnceLock sink, and start_span, which returns None whenever no sink is installed or the installed sink reports itself disabled — so with telemetry off every instrumentation site costs one branch. Redaction is structural rather than a filter list: Attribute admits only &'static str keys with integer, boolean or &'static str values, so no query, content, conversation id, token, path or model name can be attached to a span at all. crates/hm-serve/src/telemetry.rs supplies TelemetryMode, the single re-pointable FileSpanSink, configure, flush and shutdown; the sink buffers records under a mutex, appends one OTLP resourceSpans JSON object per line to an owner-only file, and sync_alls on flush. The daemon emits hypermind.request around the existing handle_request call in uds.rs, reusing the already-&'static str request_name label and resolving a tool verb to a &'static str through rest::VERBS so an unknown verb records 'unknown' instead of caller-supplied text."
do_2 = "UdsServer::serve_until flushes before returning, and hm serve gains --telemetry-file and --telemetry-service, calling configure before binding and flush after the listeners join. Telemetry stays off unless the flag is present."
do_3 = "Prove it: With no telemetry flag and no configure call, hm_core::telemetry::start_span returns None, no file is created, and existing crates/hm-serve/tests/* behaviour is unchanged. hm serve --help lists --telemetry-file and --telemetry-service; neither has a default that enables export."

[task.11.4]
title = "Ingestion, extraction and provider spans on the installed sink"
status = "done"
wave = 11
owner_lane = "cognition"
requires = ["11.3"]
reqs = ["11.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/telemetry.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/dispute.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/reconstruct.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/reconstruction_surface.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/telemetry_spans.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test telemetry_spans --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Extend the span coverage established in g11-t3 from the request edge down through the three remaining stages named by the item: ingestion, extraction and provider. Ingestion spans wrap ActorEngine::append and ActorEngine::append_idempotent in crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs, recording the actor id and the event count as integers and the outcome — covering the daemon Append path, the MCP remember path and the embedded CLI path in one place. Extraction spans wrap the ConsolidateAction::Run arm of crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/consolidate.rs, recording a static mode label and, on success, the run's declared cost counters read back from the returned envelope's cost and stats objects."
do_2 = "Provider spans come from a decorator: crates/hm-mcp/src/telemetry.rs defines ObservedProvider, a real hm_llm::LlmProvider implementation that delegates to an inner provider and records hypermind.provider with the model tier as a static label and the token counts and cost as integers. It is applied once at each runtime constructor — ConsolidationRuntime::new, DisputeRuntime::new and a new ReconstructionRuntime::new that replaces the public field — so every consolidation, dispute and reconstruction call made anywhere beneath hm-mcp is instrumented without touching hm-cortex or hm-compose. The model id and prompt never enter a span; only the tier, counts and outcome do."
do_3 = "The decorator lives in hm-mcp, which already depends on both hm-core and hm-llm, so no Cargo.toml and no lockfile changes anywhere."
do_4 = "Prove it: With the file sink configured, ActorEngine::append of a two-event batch emits one span named hypermind.ingestion with hypermind.actor and hypermind.ingestion.events == 2 and status.code == 1. Cargo.lock, fuzz/Cargo.lock, sdk/python/native/Cargo.lock and sdk/typescript/packages/engine/native/Cargo.lock are unchanged."

[task.11.5]
title = "Progressive capability discovery as a mode inside inspect"
status = "done"
wave = 11
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = []
reqs = ["11.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/surfaces.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/discovery.rs", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/tools/usage.json", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-mcp --test discovery --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Keep the advertised MCP tool surface at fourteen verbs while letting the capability catalogue grow, by adding a discovery mode inside the existing inspect verb. crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/surfaces.rs introduces a static catalogue of twenty-eight capability surfaces, each naming its verb, its <verb>.<surface> id, a one-line summary, the argument shape an agent would send, whether it mutates, which runtime or token it requires, and a small keyword list for matching. InspectInput gains mode (defaulting to the current status behaviour so every existing caller and test is unaffected), query and limit. In discover mode tools::inspect::run returns before touching the ledger: it ranks the catalogue with a deterministic lexical scorer over verb, surface id, summary and keywords, clamps the limit between one and sixty-four with a default of twelve, and returns one item per matching surface annotated with available and unavailable_reason derived from the server's real runtime state."
do_2 = "Availability is advisory only: unavailable and privileged surfaces are still listed, every discovery envelope carries the discovery_is_not_authorization warning, and no capability check moves out of dispatch. The verb inventory, the dispatcher table, the wire allowlist, the REST VERBS array and the docs catalogue's fourteen-verb header are all untouched."
do_3 = "Prove it: McpServer::tool_router().list_all() still yields exactly the fourteen existing names; hm_serve::rest::VERBS.len() == 14; crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs is unchanged. Discovery performs no ledger read: the discover branch is taken before actor.stats() and actor.verification_status()."

[task.11.6]
title = "Discovery through the daemon, and proof that discovery grants nothing"
status = "done"
wave = 11
owner_lane = "kernel-edge"
requires = ["11.5"]
reqs = ["11.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/tests/discovery_surface.rs", "docs/reference/mcp.md", "docs/reference/generated/tools.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve --test discovery_surface --locked && node docs/tools/catalog.mjs --check"
do_1 = "Carry the discovery surface from g11-t5 out through the real daemon and prove the non-authorization property end to end, so the group closes with a runnable capability rather than a library feature. A new integration test binds a real UdsServer with the real McpToolDispatcher, authenticates an actor-token connection, and issues inspect in discover mode as an ordinary ToolRequest — the same path REST and gRPC take — asserting the returned envelope enumerates privileged surfaces the caller cannot invoke. It then invokes one of those discovered privileged surfaces on the same connection and asserts it is refused with kCapabilityDenied and a correct effect_state, demonstrating that discovery advertised the surface without widening authority."
do_2 = "The test also pins the advertised inventory: the tool router still lists fourteen names, rest::VERBS is still fourteen entries, and the discovery catalogue count is asserted independently, so a future capability addition that tries to become a verb fails here rather than in review. Finally the group's docs claim is made concrete: the MCP reference states the invariant and the generated catalogues are regenerated and committed."
do_3 = "Prove it: Over a real Unix-socket daemon on an actor-token connection, ToolRequest { verb: 'inspect', arguments_json: {'mode':'discover','query':'forget'} } returns a BytesResult whose decoded envelope has ok == true and contains an item with surface == 'forget.crypto_shred', requires == 'admin_token' and available == false. A discovery request issued on an admin-token connection is rejected by the existing admin/actor partition exactly as any other tool request is, with no special-casing added for discovery."

[task.12.1]
title = "Source connector event vocabulary in schema, ledger frame and ingest"
status = "done"
wave = 12
section = "Wave 12 - Authorized source connectors"
owner_lane = "schema"
requires = []
reqs = ["12.1"]
touches = ["schemas/events.fbs", "crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs", "crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/src/frame.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/authority.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/ingest.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/checkpoint.rs", "crates/hm-schema/tests/connectors.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/tests/frame.rs", "docs/reference/generated/schema-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-schema -p hm-ledger"
do_1 = "Add the four source-connector ledger records to the schema so every later task in this group has a durable vocabulary to write. In schemas/events.fbs add the enums SourceSignatureScheme, SourceDeliveryState and ConnectorState, add the tables SourceConnectorBound, SourceDeliveryAccepted, SourceDeliverySettled and SourceRevisionObserved, and append those four names to union EventPayload in that order. Regenerate crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs with planus 1.3.0 (planus rust -o crates/hm-schema/src/events_generated.rs schemas/events.fbs, binary at /root/.cargo/bin/planus); never hand-edit it."
do_2 = "In crates/hm-schema/src/event.rs add EventKind discriminants 44..=47, the TryFrom<u8> arms, membership in is_wave_seven, the payload_kind arms, the validate_payload arms with one validate_source_* function per record, and the authority pins in validate_envelope beside the ProcedureAdopted rule. Mirror the same four numbers into hm_ledger::frame::EventKind and grow its KINDS array to [EventKind; 47]. Close the exhaustive matches that this forces open: hm_cortex::authority::authority_for_event, hm_cortex::ingest::ingest (plus runtime_event), and hm_proj::checkpoint::schema_kind, so a source frame is verifiable at Boundary::Disk, Boundary::Socket and inside a projection."
do_3 = "No producer and no projection are added here; the consumers are g12-t2 and g12-t5."
do_4 = "Prove it: schemas/events.fbs declares SourceSignatureScheme, SourceDeliveryState and ConnectorState and the four tables, and union EventPayload ends with SourceConnectorBound, SourceDeliveryAccepted, SourceDeliverySettled, SourceRevisionObserved in that order; the first 43 members are byte-for-byte unchanged. cargo test --locked -p hm-schema -p hm-ledger passes, including the pre-existing validation.rs, anticipation.rs and frame.rs suites unchanged apart from the widened kind range."

[task.12.2]
title = "Source connector registry projection with durable inbox and revision heads"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "projections"
requires = ["12.1"]
reqs = ["12.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-proj/src/connectors.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/store.rs", "crates/hm-proj/src/rebuild.rs", "crates/hm-proj/tests/connectors.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-proj --test connectors"
do_1 = "Add the read model that turns the four source-connector events into queryable state, so admission and the surfaces have something to check against. Create crates/hm-proj/src/connectors.rs holding ConnectorRegistryProjection with the simple-projection shape used by crates/hm-proj/src/attestations.rs: early-return store.apply(id, lsn, &[]) for unrelated kinds so the checkpoint still advances, open a snapshot, verify the frame through crate::checkpoint::verify_frame, build mutations, drop the snapshot before store.apply. Append ProjectionId::SourceConnectors as the nineteenth variant with the PROJECTION_NAMES entry 'source_connectors' and bump ProjectionId::COUNT to 19, keeping the array index and the enum discriminant aligned."
do_2 = "SourceConnectorBound writes the connector record under b'C' and the redeemed consent nonce under b'N'; SourceDeliveryAccepted writes a delivery record under b'D'; SourceDeliverySettled updates that delivery record in place with attempt, state and next_attempt_at_ns; SourceRevisionObserved replaces the revision head under b'R'. Wire the projection into rebuild_projection_stream (checkpoint read, both checkpoint arrays, the apply block, and reset_all) so a reset rebuild is byte-identical. Reads are bounded and take a ReadSnapshot only."
do_3 = "Prove it: ProjectionId::SourceConnectors exists at index 18 with name 'source_connectors', ProjectionId::COUNT is 19, and PROJECTION_NAMES has 19 entries in enum order. cargo test --locked -p hm-proj --test connectors passes and the pre-existing crates/hm-proj/tests/rebuild.rs still passes with COUNT = 19."

[task.12.3]
title = "Versioned connector credential vault under the actor key hierarchy"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "ledger"
requires = []
reqs = ["12.2"]
touches = ["crates/hm-ledger/src/credentials.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-ledger/tests/credentials.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-ledger --test credentials"
do_1 = "Give connector secrets a versioned, rotatable home that reuses the actor's existing key hierarchy instead of a second key system. Create crates/hm-ledger/src/credentials.rs with CredentialVault, a stateless helper over an actor directory whose methods take &KeyHierarchy, so it composes with WriterState's owned key hierarchy without lifetime entanglement. A credential is sealed with XChaCha20-Poly1305 under the data key with authenticated associated data binding the domain, the actor id, the user id, the credential version, the provider string and the connector id, so a secret written for one provider, actor or connector cannot be opened as another."
do_2 = "Each version is its own 0o600 file under <actor_directory>/connectors/<connector hex>/<version:010>.cred written temp-then-rename with a directory fsync using the crate's existing io_error and sync_directory helpers; storing a version that already exists is refused with kAlreadyExists, which is what makes rotation additive and keeps every prior version decryptable. Also expose consent_key, a blake3 keyed derivation from the data key for the consent-state tag, mirroring how checkpoint.rs derives its signing key pair. Nothing here touches the log, so key rotation re-wrapping the data key leaves every stored credential readable, and crypto-shred makes them permanently unreadable."
do_3 = "Prove it: CredentialVault::open creates <actor_directory>/connectors with mode 0o700 and returns kKeyDestroyed-safe behaviour by deferring to the caller's KeyHierarchy (which already refuses after a deletion receipt). cargo test --locked -p hm-ledger --test credentials passes."

[task.12.4]
title = "Delivery signature verification, single-use consent state and retry policy"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "cortex"
requires = []
reqs = ["12.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/connectors/mod.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/connectors.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-cortex --test connectors"
do_1 = "Add the pure admission logic for signed external sources beside the existing per-turn ingest rules. Create crates/hm-cortex/src/connectors.rs holding a local HMAC-SHA256 over the crate's existing sha2 dependency (no new third-party crate), the canonical delivery signing base, the freshness window check, and constant-time comparison through subtle::ConstantTimeEq. verify_delivery takes the connector secret, a DeliveryEnvelope borrowed from the caller's bytes, the actor clock and a window, and returns a VerifiedDelivery carrying the blake3 body digest and the body length; it fails with kSignatureInvalid on a tag mismatch, kOrderingViolation when signed_at_ns is outside the window, and kInvalidArgument on a body larger than MAXIMUM_DELIVERY_BYTES. mint_consent_state and verify_consent_state implement the provider- and connector-bound single-use grant: the tag is verified before any field is read, so a forged state never influences behaviour, and an expired state fails with kCapabilityDenied. retry_delay_ns and retry_exhausted give the durable inbox a bounded exponential schedule so the settlement events written later are deterministic. Everything here is a pure function of its inputs plus an explicit now_ns; no clock, no I/O, no ledger."
do_2 = "Prove it: hmac_sha256 reproduces the published RFC 4231 test-case-1 and test-case-2 vectors for SHA-256 exactly, including a key longer than the 64-byte block. retry_delay_ns(1) is 1_000_000_000, doubles per attempt and saturates at 60_000_000_000; retry_exhausted(attempt) is true exactly when attempt > MAXIMUM_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS (5)."

[task.12.5]
title = "Actor plumbing: credential custody, consent grants and source admission preconditions"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "surfaces-daemon"
requires = ["12.1", "12.2", "12.3", "12.4"]
reqs = ["12.2", "12.3"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/actor.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/connectors.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-serve --test connectors"
do_1 = "Wire the vault, the verification functions and the registry projection into the single-writer actor so no secret ever crosses the command channel and so the durable invariants hold at append time. WriterState gains a CredentialVault opened in WriterState::open right after the KeyHierarchy, and four new Command variants plus their ActorEngine async wrappers: store a credential version, verify a signed delivery (the secret is loaded, used and dropped inside the writer), mint a consent state, and redeem a consent state. Add three bounded registry reads that mirror the existing AttentionHistory and Calibration command shape and return hm_proj::connectors records from a ReadSnapshot."
do_2 = "Extend WriterState::validate_anticipation with the four source arms so single use, inbox idempotency and connector authorization are enforced at admission rather than only at the surface: a SourceConnectorBound whose consent nonce is already redeemed is kIdempotencyConflict; a SourceDeliveryAccepted for an unbound or revoked connector is kCapabilityDenied and for a delivery_id already present is kIdempotencyConflict; a SourceDeliverySettled without a matching accepted delivery, or whose attempt does not advance, is kOrderingViolation; a SourceRevisionObserved for an unbound or revoked connector is kCapabilityDenied. Extend the in-batch duplicate key set in WriterState::append so two deliveries with the same id inside one batch are rejected too."
do_3 = "Prove it: ActorEngine::store_connector_credential persists a version through CredentialVault and returns kAlreadyExists when the same version is stored twice. cargo test --locked -p hm-serve --test connectors passes."

[task.12.6]
title = "Connector lifecycle inside the bind verb and registry reads inside inspect"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "surfaces-mcp"
requires = ["12.5"]
reqs = ["12.2", "12.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/connector.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/bind.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/connectors.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test connectors"
do_1 = "Surface the connector lifecycle without adding a fifteenth MCP verb. BindInput gains an optional connector object; when present, tools::bind::run short-circuits into a new tools::connector module exactly the way recall short-circuits into tools::reconstruct, so the existing task and scope binding path is untouched. The connector action vocabulary is consent (mint a single-use state for a provider and connector), bind (redeem that state, store the supplied signing secret at credential_version through ActorEngine::store_connector_credential, then append one SourceConnectorBound with authority user_asserted and state bound), rotate (store the next credential version and append a SourceConnectorBound that carries the new credential_version and keeps state bound), and revoke (append a SourceConnectorBound with state revoked)."
do_2 = "Every append goes through ActorEngine::append, so the admission preconditions from g12-t5 are the durable guard and the tool only shapes and reports. InspectInput gains no new field: inspect resolves hm://<actor>/connectors through ActorEngine::connectors and renders provider, external account, credential version, scopes, state and the binding LSN with a provenance URI per record. The envelope never echoes the secret or the consent tag."
do_3 = "Prove it: bind with action consent returns an envelope whose single item carries the encoded state, the nonce hex and expires_at_ns, performs no append, and reports no effect_state. cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test connectors passes."

[task.12.7]
title = "Signed delivery admission and settlement inside the remember verb"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "surfaces-mcp"
requires = ["12.5", "12.6"]
reqs = ["12.3", "12.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/source.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/mod.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/source_inbox.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test source_inbox"
do_1 = "Make the durable inbox reachable. RememberInput gains two optional objects, source_delivery and source_settlement, and remember_inner short-circuits into a new tools::source module before its existing content validation, so the ordinary remember path is untouched. A delivery is admitted by verifying the signature through ActorEngine::verify_source_delivery against the connector's stored credential version and then appending two events in one batch: a SourceDeliveryAccepted carrying the blake3 body digest, and a ProviderFrame carrying the verified body so the content itself lands in the ledger as external_observed evidence rather than as a bare digest."
do_2 = "A repeat of the same delivery_id is not an error: the tool reads the registry first and returns the prior accepted_lsn with duplicate true, which is the same contract the idempotent append path already offers, while the actor precondition remains the durable backstop. A settlement appends one SourceDeliverySettled with the caller's attempt and outcome, filling next_attempt_at_ns from hm_cortex::connectors::retry_delay_ns and forcing state abandoned once retry_exhausted. inspect resolves hm://<actor>/inbox, listing recent deliveries with their state, attempt and next attempt time."
do_3 = "Prove it: remember with source_delivery and a correct signature appends exactly two events, returns accepted_lsn, body_lsn, body_digest hex and duplicate false, and pushes one hm://<actor>/lsn/<n> provenance URI per event. cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test source_inbox passes."

[task.12.8]
title = "Source transport seam and revision listing driver"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "cortex"
requires = ["12.4"]
reqs = ["12.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-cortex/src/connectors/mod.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/src/connectors/sync.rs", "crates/hm-cortex/tests/source_sync.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-cortex --test source_sync"
do_1 = "Give repository and workspace sync an outbound seam that is testable without a live service, modelled exactly on the recorded wire transports already used for embedding and LLM providers. Add crates/hm-cortex/src/connectors/sync.rs (moving connectors.rs to connectors/mod.rs and re-exporting, or keeping a flat module plus a sync submodule) with SourceRequest, SourceResponse and the blocking SourceTransport trait, plus RecordedSourceTransport which pops an ordered fixture list, asserts exact SourceRequest equality and exposes remaining(), and HttpSourceTransport built on the crate's existing blocking reqwest dependency with an explicit timeout. list_revisions issues one request per page against HyperMind's own source-index contract, a JSON object {'sources':[{'source_id':..,'revision':..,'content_digest':..}],'next_cursor':..}, validates every field defensively (non-empty source_id and revision, a 64-character lowercase hex content digest), bounds the walk at MAXIMUM_SOURCE_PAGES and MAXIMUM_SOURCE_IDS, and returns SourceRevisionListing values ready to become ledger records."
do_2 = "A non-2xx status, a malformed body or an unbounded cursor loop is an error, never a partial success. The consumer is g12-t9."
do_3 = "Prove it: list_revisions against a RecordedSourceTransport holding one page returns the listed revisions in order with decoded 32-byte content digests, and transport().remaining() == 0 afterwards. cargo test --locked -p hm-cortex --test source_sync passes."

[task.12.9]
title = "Authorized source sync into revision records inside the remember verb"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "surfaces-mcp"
requires = ["12.7", "12.8"]
reqs = ["12.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/source.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/remember.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/lib.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/dispatcher.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/src/tools/inspect.rs", "crates/hm-mcp/tests/source_sync.rs", "docs/reference/generated/rust-types.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test source_sync"
do_1 = "Close the pull half of the connector. RememberInput gains an optional source_sync object; remember_inner short-circuits into tools::source::sync, which refuses unless a SourceRuntime is configured, checks that the named connector is bound and not revoked through ActorEngine::connectors, lists revisions through hm_cortex::connectors::sync::list_revisions inside tokio::task::spawn_blocking (the same way the embedding runtime wraps its blocking work), skips any source whose revision already matches the stored head, and appends one SourceRevisionObserved per changed source in a single batch with authority external_observed."
do_2 = "The runtime is added to McpServer with with_source_runtime and to McpToolDispatcher::from_env behind HM_SOURCE_TRANSPORT, so an unconfigured daemon answers kOperationUnavailable rather than reaching the network, exactly like the reconstruction and consolidation runtimes. inspect resolves hm://<actor>/revisions to list the stored heads. The access token is read from the connector's stored credential inside the actor and never appears in an argument, an item or a warning."
do_3 = "Prove it: remember with source_sync and no configured SourceRuntime returns ok false with kOperationUnavailable and effect_state 'not_dispatched'; no append occurs. cargo test --locked -p hm-mcp --test source_sync passes."

[task.12.10]
title = "Connector documentation, tool usage guidance and a green docs gate"
status = "done"
wave = 12
owner_lane = "docs"
requires = ["12.6", "12.7", "12.9"]
reqs = ["12.1", "12.4"]
