do_1 = "Close the group with the documentation the gate demands and the prose an operator needs. Write docs/concepts/connectors.md covering the connector as an actor-bound authorization, the four ledger records and their pinned authority classes, the single-use consent grant, versioned and rotatable credentials under the actor key hierarchy, the durable inbox with its idempotency key and bounded retry schedule, and the revision heads; link it from docs/SUMMARY.md so the mdBook build and the link checker both pass. Refresh docs/tools/usage.json for bind, remember and inspect so their when, avoid and example entries show the connector surfaces, and add the do-not-use guidance the documentation contract requires."
do_2 = "Regenerate every catalog once more and run the full gate so the group ends with byte-exact generated pages. Record honestly in the page what is not covered here: the checked-in Go and TypeScript FlatBuffers event trees are not regenerated, and HttpSourceTransport has no test in this environment."
do_3 = "Prove it: docs/concepts/connectors.md exists, is linked from docs/SUMMARY.md, and its internal links and anchors resolve under the checkout. The page states, in HyperMind's own words, that the Go and TypeScript wire event trees and the live HTTP source transport are outside this group's verified scope."

[task.13.1]
title = "Serve console assets from the REST actor listener"
status = "done"
wave = 13
section = "Wave 13 - The console"
owner_lane = "surfaces"
requires = []
reqs = ["13.4"]
touches = ["crates/hm-serve/src/rest/mod.rs", "crates/hm-cli/src/serve.rs", "crates/hm-serve/tests/console.rs", "docs/reference/generated/cli-declarations.md", "docs/reference/generated/coverage.json"]
verify_cmd = "cargo test -p hm-serve -p hm-cli console"
do_1 = "Give the console a serving path before it exists. Add two GET routes to the existing axum router in crates/hm-serve/src/rest/mod.rs: GET /console returns index.html from a configured directory, and GET /console/{file} returns one flat asset from that same directory. The directory is supplied by a new builder RestServer::with_console_directory and, at the command line, by a new hm serve --console-directory PATH option on RemoteOptions that requires --rest-bind."
do_2 = "Asset serving is not a data surface: it is refused on the admin listener, it never touches the daemon gateway, and it is deliberately left out of the utoipa document and schemas/openapi.yaml so the fourteen verb paths and their asserted mirror stay exactly as they are. File names are validated against a strict allowlist and mapped to a fixed content-type table, so no path outside the configured directory and no unexpected media type can be served. When no console directory is configured every console route answers 404, which is the state of every existing deployment."
do_3 = "Prove it: GET /console on an actor-role REST listener configured with a console directory returns 200, content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8, cache-control: no-store, and a body byte-identical to index.html in that directory. schemas/openapi.yaml and hm_serve::rest::VERBS are unchanged, and crates/hm-serve/tests/remote.rs still passes unmodified."

